{"level":30,"time":1776969540549,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JzwqGC6awBNdpQzNPvBmo4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by understanding the task:\n\n1. I need to complete ONE grouping file which contains MULTIPLE related checklist items\n2. My grouping file is: `/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/review-guides/el-md-exp/2.md`\n3. I need to process all checklist items in this grouping, then stop\n4. I need to return findings in a specific structured format\n\nLet me follow the workflow:\n\n## Step 1: Read the Grouping File\nFirst, I need to read the grouping file to understand:\n- Description\n- Regulatory Overview\n- Code References\n- Documents to Review\n- Checklist Items Table\n- Code Citation column\n\n## Step 2: Check Applicability\n- Review the Description\n- Check facts.md and README for relevant infrastructure/features\n- Check regulating plan if applicable\n\n## Step 3: Research Phase\n- Gather evidence relevant to the entire grouping topic\n- Use site plan navigation pattern\n- Check supplementary documents\n\n## Step 4: Evaluate Each Checklist Item\n- Determine status: pass, fail, n/a, or not-verifiable\n\n## Step 5: Return Findings\n- Only include fail and not-verifiable items\n- Use structured output format\n\nLet me start by reading the grouping file.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23755,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23755},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"970d0b0f-6cb0-49b0-933a-a570c2e8fa2d","uuid":"664b28