{"level":30,"time":1776969552743,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01A2AiceMBfe2Vd6hURhtnD1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent. I have the facts. Let me note key findings:\n\n1. **Project:** Valley View Townhomes - a 39-unit multi-family townhome development with 8 buildings\n2. **Site Area:** 2.16 acres (with discrepancies noted)\n3. **Utilities:** The site has existing utilities including electric infrastructure (noted as \"5 Electric Easements\")\n4. **Landscape:** The project includes extensive landscape work - I can see Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan), Sheet 30 (Existing Tree Plan), Sheet 32 (Tree List), and Sheet 35-37 (Landscape Details)\n\nThe facts.md references:\n- \"Easement 7 & 8 — 5' Electric Easements (×2)\" and \"Easement 9 — 7.5' Public Utility Easement\" which are plat-dedicated\n\nSheet 21 is \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" which should show the electric infrastructure.\n\nThis grouping (EL-2) is about tree clearances from overhead electric lines. So I need to check:\n\n1. Do overhead electric distribution/transmission lines exist on the site?\n2. Are trees proposed in the landscape plan?\n3. Are the tree placements compliant with clearance requirements?\n\nLet me start by examining the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and the landscape plan (Sheet 31) to understand the site's electrical infrastructure and proposed trees.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8440,"cache_read_input_tokens":27266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8440},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21547d2b-78a2-4a78-a9a7-59