{"level":30,"time":1776969588084,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Identify and document all transformer pad locations on this electrical design plan. For each transformer, provide: 1) Its location (describe relative to buildings/site features), 2) Dimensions if labeled, 3) Proximity to buildings, structures, sidewalks, parking areas, trees, utilities, or other site features. Also note the scale of the drawing and whether clearance dimensions are dimensioned or could be measured. Identify service type if specified (single-phase or three-phase).","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for \"Valley View Townhomes\", here is the documentation regarding transformer pad locations as requested.\n\n### General Drawing Information\n*   **Scale:** The drawing includes a graphic scale in the top right corner indicating **Scale 1\" = 20'**.\n*   **Clearance Dimensions:** There are no explicit dimensional callouts (text indicating specific distances like 5', 10', etc.) showing required clearances around the transformer pads from buildings, vegetation, or other structures. However, because the drawing is to scale (1\" = 20'), clearances *could be measured* using the scale.\n*   **Service Type:** The plan does not explicitly specify whether the service is single-phase or three-phase on this specific sheet.\n*   **Dimensions:** None of the transformer pads have explicit text dimensions (e.g., 6'x6') labeled on them.\n\n---\n\n### Transformer Pad Locations\n\nI have identified 4 separate transformer pads on this site plan. They are explicitly labeled as \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" inside blue boxes pointing to rectangular pad symbols.\n\n**1. Northwest Transformer Pad (Near Bldg 2)**\n*   **Label:** \"Electrical Transformer Pad\"\n*   **Location:** Located on the western edge of the site, north of the main entrance drive aisle.\n*   **Dimensions:** Not labeled.\n*   **Proximity to Site Features:**\n    *   **Buildings:** Situated directly west of Building 2 (near Unit 201).\n    *   **Sidewalks/Curbs:** Located immediately east of a curved sidewalk and the western boundary curb.\n    *   **Trees:** The pad is drawn directly underneath the canopy of large existing trees.\n    *   **Utilities:** It connects via underground blue electrical lines to an \"Electrical Pull Box\" to its south, which then branches to \"Electrical Meters\" for Bldg 1 and Bldg 2.\n\n**2. East Central Transformer Pad (Between Bldg 4 & Bldg 5)**\n*   **Label:** \"Electrical Transformer Pad\"\n*   **Location:** Located in the eastern portion of the site, situated in the open space between two buildings.\n*   **Dimensions:** Not labeled.\n*   **Proximity to Site Features:**\n    *   **Buildings:** Located east of Building 4 (near Unit 404) and west of Building 5 (near Units 503/504).\n    *   **Trees:** The pad is drawn partially underneath/adjacent to large tree canopies.\n    *   **Utilities:** It is connected to an \"Electrical Pull Box\" located slightly to its north. Underground lines route from this area to \"Electrical Meters\" on Bldg 4 and Bldg 5. Sanitary sewer (\"SD\") lines run nearby.\n\n**3. Southwest Transformer Pad (Near Bldg 8)**\n*   **Label:** \"Electrical Transformer Pad\"\n*   **Location:** Located in the southwest corner area of the development.\n*   **Dimensions:** Not labeled.\n*   **Proximity to Site Features:**\n    *   **Buildings:** Located directly west of Building 8 (near Unit 801).\n    *   **Sidewalks/Easements:** Situated just inside the property line, east of a designated \"Sidewalk Easement\" running along the western boundary.\n    *   **Trees:** The pad is drawn directly underneath a large tree canopy.\n    *   **Utilities:** An \"Underground Electric Line\" comes from off-site to the west, connects near the pad, and feeds an \"Electrical Pull Box\" immediately to the south. Lines then run to \"Electrical Meters\" on Bldg 8. It is also located near a \"Vault Easement\".\n\n**4. Southeast Transformer Pad (Between Bldg 6 & Bldg 7)**\n*   **Label:** \"Electrical Transformer Pad\"\n*   **Location:** Located in the south-central/eastern area of the site, between two buildings and east of the central drive aisle.\n*   **Dimensions:** Not labeled.\n*   **Proximity to Site Features:**\n    *   **Buildings:** Located south of Building 7 (near Unit 703) and north of Building 6 (near Unit 602).\n    *   **Driveways/Parking:** Situated to the east of the primary central driveway/parking area.\n    *   **Trees:** The pad is drawn directly underneath/adjacent to a large tree canopy.\n    *   **Utilities:** Connects to an \"Electrical Pull Box\" located slightly to its southwest. Lines run to \"Electrical Meters\" on Bldg 6 and Bldg 7. A fire hydrant (\"FH\") is located to the southwest near the pull box.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1408,"outputTokens":999,"totalTokens":4100,"reasoningTokens":1693},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the 