{"level":30,"time":1776969602011,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Analyze the landscape plan on Sheet 31 and identify:\n1. All tree locations shown on the plan (use the tree symbols: circles with dots, crosses, hash marks, wavy edges, jagged edges)\n2. The location of overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the plan\n3. The approximate distance/proximity between any trees and the overhead electric lines\n4. Any utility poles or electric equipment shown on the landscape plan\n5. Any labels or notes related to tree clearances from utilities\n\nPlease provide a detailed description of the tree placement relative to overhead electric infrastructure, including which areas of the site have trees near utilities and which areas have trees away from utilities.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (which is labeled as Sheet **28 of 35** in the bottom right corner, despite the prompt's reference to Sheet 31), here are the findings regarding your specific requirements:\n\n**1. Tree Locations Shown on the Plan**\nTrees are primarily located along the perimeter of the property, with specific concentrations:\n*   **Northern Boundary (Top):** A continuous row of large canopy trees (represented by large circles with dots or crosses in the center) runs along the entire northern edge of the site plan.\n*   **Western Boundary (Left):** Several trees are located within the shaded gray area along the left side of the buildings, designated by key note \"H.2\" as \"STREET YARD\". Some of these trees carry labels like \"SY\" (Street Yard Tree) and \"M\" (Mitigation Tree).\n*   **Southern Boundary (Bottom):** A continuous row of approximately 8-9 trees (represented by circles with various internal line markings) runs along the southern edge of the property line.\n*   **Eastern Boundary (Right):** A few scattered trees are located near the northeastern and southeastern corners, as well as a couple adjacent to the eastern \"FILTRATION BASIN\" and \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\".\n*   **Interior Areas:** There are relatively few trees in the interior courtyards/drive isles, with most planting focused on the outer perimeter.\n\n**2. Location of Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines**\n*   An overhead electric line is shown running continuously along the **southern boundary** (bottom edge) of the site plan.\n*   It is explicitly denoted by a distinct line type consisting of long dashes separated by the text label **\"-OHE-\"**.\n\n**3. Approximate Distance/Proximity Between Trees and OHE Lines**\n*   **Southern Boundary Intersections:** The row of trees planted along the southern property line is positioned in direct conflict with the overhead electric infrastructure.\n*   The \"-OHE-\" line passes directly through the circular symbols representing the tree canopies. Based on the \"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\" provided, the center points (trunks) of these trees appear to be planted within 0 to 10 feet of the OHE line, with their mature canopies shown overlapping the utility line directly.\n*   **Away from Utilities:** The trees along the northern, western, and eastern boundaries are located far away from the indicated \"-OHE-\" line on the southern border and do not appear to have overhead utility conflicts based on this specific sheet.\n\n**4. Utility Poles or Electric Equipment Shown**\n*   While not explicitly defined in the \"KEY NOTES\" legend, there are small circular symbols with crosshairs located at the far southwestern (bottom-left) and southeastern (bottom-right) ends of the \"-OHE-\" line, which typically represent utility poles.\n*   No large electrical equipment pads (like transformers) are clearly labeled or visible in the landscaped areas on this specific sheet.\n\n**5. Labels or Notes Related to Tree Clearances from Utilities**\n*   **None found.** I have reviewed the \"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE\" section, \"KEY NOTES\", and the tree abbreviation legend (SY, PL, P, M) on the right side of the document. There are no notes, disclaimers, or labels providing instructions regarding minimum planting distances or canopy clearances from overhead electric lines.\n\n**Summary of Tree Placement Relative to Overhead Electric Infrastructure:**\nThe site strategy places a dense buffer of trees along the entire perimeter of the property. The trees on the North, East, and West sides are positioned away from indicated overhead utilities. However, the landscaping along the South side features a row of trees planted directly underneath or immediately adjacent to the \"-OHE-\" line, with their canopy symbols shown visually overlapping the utility line. There are no notes on this sheet addressing this apparent utility conflict.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1449,"outputTokens":819,"totalTokens":4013,"reasoningTokens":1745},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the prima