{"level":30,"time":1776969603275,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MidgcTHTMMCcjjtH7wtkcj","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n     2→\n     3→This page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n    11→- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n    12→- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n    13→- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n    14→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n    15→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n    16→- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    19→- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n    20→- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n    21→- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n    22→- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n    23→- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n    28→\n    29→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    30→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ccf424f-5fd8-4631-ab14-3396e8bf729c","uuid":"392251cd-4605-4de3-80e9-e361b32bd3c6","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n\nThis page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n\n**Key values**:\n- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776969603308,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Carefully examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and answer the following:\n\n1. OVERHEAD ELECTRIC LINES: Where are the overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan? Describe their location(s) on the site, orientation, and any poles or infrastructure visible.\n\n2. TREE LOCATIONS: Where are trees indicated on this plan? List the general locations of tree groupings or concentrations (e.g., \"north side\", \"eastern parking area\", \"building peripheries\").\n\n3. CLEARANCE ASSESSMENT: For any trees visible near overhead electric lines, estimate approximate horizontal distances between:\n   - The trees and the OHE lines/poles\n   - Note whether these appear to be within 15 feet, 25 feet, or greater distances from the lines\n\n4. TREE SYMBOLS AND MARKING: What symbols are used to indicate different tree types? Can you identify whether specific trees are marked as \"large\" or special-sized categories that would need mature height verification?\n\n5. LANDSCAPE PLAN COMPLETENESS: Does the plan show both the overhead electric lines AND the proposed tree locations with sufficient clarity to verify clearances?\n\nContext: The site is a 2.16-acre townhome development with 8 buildings. The regulatory requirement is to ensure utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution conductors and 50 feet of transmission conductors, and large trees (mature height ≥40 feet per ECM Appendix F) within 25 feet of distribution conductors.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (noted as Sheet 28 of 35 in the bottom right corner, despite the prompt mentioning Sheet 31), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1. OVERHEAD ELECTRIC LINES:**\n*   **Location & Orientation:** Overhead electric lines are explicitly indicated along the entire bottom edge (Southern boundary) of the site plan.\n*   **Markings:** The line is designated with the text \"**- OHE -**\" interrupting a solid line running horizontally across the bottom property boundary. \n*   **Infrastructure:** While the continuous wire line is clearly marked, specific utility pole locations (typically represented by small circles or squares on the line) are not distinctly labeled or visually obvious on this specific sheet without a magnifying closer view of overlapping line weights. The line itself serves as the primary reference for the overhead utility path.\n\n**2. TREE LOCATIONS:**\nTrees are indicated extensively throughout the site plan. General concentrations include:\n*   **North side (Top boundary):** A dense row of trees runs horizontally along the upper edge, just inside the \"LOC\" (Limits of Construction) line.\n*   **West side (Left boundary):** A significant concentration of trees is located within a grey shaded area labeled with keynotes \"H-1\" (PROPOSED PAVING), \"H-2\" (STREET YARD), and \"H-3\" (STREET YARD LANDSCAPING).\n*   **East side (Right boundary):** A row of trees is positioned along the right-hand property line, primarily near the top and bottom corners.\n*   **South side (Bottom boundary):** Several trees are planted in a linear fashion along the southern edge, directly adjacent to the OHE lines.\n*   **Interior:** Trees are strategically placed around the building peripheries and within parking areas (e.g., adjacent to standard parking spaces and inside designated \"H-4\" PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING islands).\n\n**3. CLEARANCE ASSESSMENT (Trees vs. OHE Lines):**\nFocusing on the southern boundary where the \"- OHE -\" line is located:\n*   There are approximately 6 to 8 tree symbols plotted directly along this southern corridor.\n*   Based on the provided graphic scale (1\" = 20'-0\"), the center marks (representing the trunks) of several of these trees appear to be **within 5 to 10 feet** of the OHE line. \n*   The large circles representing the mature canopies of these trees significantly overlap the OHE line.\n*   **Conclusion:** Multiple proposed trees along the southern boundary are definitively plotted **within 15 feet** of the indicated overhead electric lines.\n\n**4. TREE SYMBOLS AND MARKING:**\n*   **Symbols Used:** The plan uses various circles to represent trees, primarily circles with a cross/plus sign in the center (indicating the trunk location and canopy spread), and smaller solid black circles with white crosses.\n*   **Labels:** Many trees are accompanied by alphanumeric labels. The KEY NOTES define these as:\n    *   **SY** - \"STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH...)\"\n    *   **PL** - \"PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH...)\"\n    *   **P** - \"PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n    *   **M** - \"MITIGATION TREE\"\n*   **Mature Height Verification:** This specific sheet does **not** identify whether specific trees are categorized as \"large\" (mature height ≥40 feet). It categorizes them by their regulatory function (Street Yard, Mitigation, etc.) and minimum caliper inches (e.g., 1.5 CAL. INCH). To verify utility compatibility and mature height for the 15-foot vs. 25-foot clearance rules, a separate \"Plant Schedule\" or \"Tree Schedule\" detailing the specific botanical species for each symbol would be required.\n\n**5. LANDSCAPE PLAN COMPLETENESS:**\n*   **Yes, the plan is sufficiently clear for an initial clearance assessment.** It successfully shows both the \"- OHE -\" lines and the proposed tree trunk locations (center crosses) drawn to scale.\n*   Because the plan illustrates trunk locations that measure under 15 feet from the OHE line along the southern boundary, a reviewer can confidently use this sheet to flag a potential conflict with the utility-compatible tree requirements. However, as noted above, a corresponding plant list is needed to determine the exact species and mature heights to fully adjudicate the conflict.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1620,"outputTokens":968,"totalTokens":4411,"reasoningTokens":1823},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Carefully examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and answer the following:\n\n1. OVERHEAD ELECTRIC LINES: Where are the overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan? Describe their location(s) on the site, orientation, and any poles or infrastructure visible.\n\n2. TREE LOCATIONS: Where are trees indicated on this plan? List the general locations of tree groupings or concentrations (