{"level":30,"time":1776969859790,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Analyze the electrical design plan to identify: (1) Type of electric infrastructure - are there underground lines, transformers, pad-mounted equipment, or other electric facilities shown? (2) Locations of all electrical equipment (transformers, pull boxes, meters); (3) Are overhead electric distribution or transmission lines shown on this plan? (4) Are there utility easements depicted? Provide details on what electric infrastructure is present and whether overhead lines are depicted.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for Valley View Townhomes, here are the details regarding the electrical infrastructure:\n\n**(1) Type of Electric Infrastructure**\nThe plan depicts a comprehensive underground electrical distribution network along with pad-mounted equipment. Specific infrastructure types explicitly labeled via callouts (pointing to blue-lined features) include:\n*   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: Depicted as solid blue lines routing electrical service throughout the site.\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Pad-mounted electrical transformers.\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Underground/flush-mounted pull boxes located at junction points.\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: Meter banks servicing the individual building units.\n\n**(2) Locations of all Electrical Equipment**\nThe electrical equipment is distributed throughout the site to service Buildings 1 through 8. Their specific locations, as marked by callouts, are:\n\n*   **Transformers (\"Electrical Transformer Pad\")**: There are three labeled transformer pads.\n    1.  West side of the property, located between Building 2 and Building 8, near the western \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n    2.  Central portion of the property, situated between Building 4, Building 5, Building 6, and Building 7.\n    3.  East side of the property, adjacent to the south/west corner of Building 6.\n*   **Pull Boxes (\"Electrical Pull Box\")**: There are multiple pull boxes located along the solid blue \"Underground Electric Line\" routing.\n    1.  Near the west property line where the main \"Underground Electric Line\" enters.\n    2.  Northwest area near Building 1.\n    3.  West-central area between Building 2 and Building 8.\n    4.  Southwest area near Building 8.\n    5.  Central area near Building 4 and Building 7.\n    6.  North-central area near Building 5.\n    7.  East area near Building 6.\n    8.  South property line edge, south of Building 7.\n*   **Meters (\"Electrical Meters\")**: Meter banks are located adjacent to every major building structure on the site. Callouts for \"Electrical Meters\" point to equipment immediately attached or adjacent to:\n    1.  Building 1\n    2.  Building 2\n    3.  Building 3\n    4.  Building 4\n    5.  Building 5\n    6.  Building 6\n    7.  Building 7\n    8.  Building 8\n\n**(3) Overhead Electric Distribution Lines**\n**Yes**, overhead electric lines are shown on this plan. They are depicted using a dashed linetype with the text **\"-OHE-\"** running through it. These lines are found along the perimeters of the site:\n*   Running along the western property boundary.\n*   Running along the southern property boundary.\n*   Running along the eastern property boundary.\n\n**(4) Utility Easements Depicted**\n**Yes**, there are multiple utility easements depicted and labeled on the plan. Examples of those specifically related to utilities/electrical include:\n*   **\"5' P.U.E.\"** (Public Utility Easement) noted near the northern boundary curve.\n*   **\"10' P.U.E.\"** noted in the northwest corner area.\n*   **\"5' Electric, Telephone...\"** (text partially obscured) noted along the eastern boundary.\n*   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 385 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"** noted in the southeast corner.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1400,"outputTokens":784,"totalTokens":3929,"reasoningTokens":1745},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Analyze the electrical design plan to identify: (1) Type of electric infrastructure - are there underground lines, transformers, pad-mounted equipment, or other electric facilities shown? (2) Locations of all electrical equipment (transformers, pull boxes, meters); (3) Are overhead electric distribution or transmission lines shown on this plan? (4) Are there utility easements depicted? Provide details on what electric infrastructure is present and whether overhead lines are depicted."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-LcF4ydGGmbSljyFAcv5uMFfn","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 18:40:35 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::z25kd-1776969592479-d6df8cad6e42"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for Valley View Townhomes, here are the details regarding the electrical infrastructure:\n\n**(1) Type of Electric Infrastructure**\nThe plan depicts a comprehensive underground electrical distribution network along with pad-mounted equipment. Specific infrastructure types explicitly labeled via callouts (pointing to blue-lined features) include:\n*   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: Depicted as solid blue lines routing electrical service throughout the site.\n*   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Pad-mounted electrical transformers.\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Underground/flush-mounted pull boxes