{"level":30,"time":1776969859831,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the electrical design plan on Sheet 21 and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. The location and nature of all electric utility infrastructure shown:\n   - Are there overhead electric lines on the property? If yes, where are they located?\n   - Are there utility poles shown on the site plan? If yes, how many and where?\n   - Are there pad-mounted transformers or electrical equipment on the site? If yes, where?\n   - Are electric lines underground or overhead? Provide locations for both if applicable.\n\n2. Voltage classification and line type:\n   - What voltage class are the utility lines (distribution vs. transmission)?\n   - What labels or markings indicate this?\n\n3. Spatial relationship with proposed buildings:\n   - How close are any overhead lines to the buildings?\n   - Are there any notes about clearances or setbacks?\n\n4. Any notes about tree clearances or utility compatibility:\n   - Are there any notes or symbols indicating restrictions on tree planting near utilities?\n   - Any references to Austin Energy approvals or conditions?\n\nPlease be specific about locations (north, south, east, west, interior, perimeter) and provide measurements where scale permits.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 21, \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here is the requested information:\n\n**1. Location and nature of all electric utility infrastructure shown:**\n\n*   **Overhead electric lines:** Yes, there are overhead electric lines.\n    *   *Western Perimeter:* A line labeled repeatedly as **\"-OHE-\"** runs generally north-south along the western boundary of the site, adjacent to what appears to be \"Valley View Road\".\n    *   *Southern Perimeter:* Another line labeled **\"-OHE-\"** runs generally east-west just outside the southern property line boundary.\n*   **Utility poles:** Yes.\n    *   Near the northwest corner of the property lines, there is a faint symbol pointing to a circle on the overhead line that appears to be an existing utility pole. While circles appear along the \"-OHE-\" lines at directional changes, specific textual labels for \"utility pole\" are sparse; one is faintly visible in the upper-left quadrant near the existing wastewater easement.\n*   **Pad-mounted transformers or electrical equipment:** Yes, several pieces of electrical equipment are explicitly labeled on the site plan (represented by blue boxes):\n    *   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Three are clearly labeled.\n        *   One on the west side, south of Building 1.\n        *   One on the east side, east of Building 4.\n        *   One on the west side, south of Building 8.\n    *   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Several are labeled throughout the site, primarily located along the interior driveways connecting the underground network (e.g., near Bldg 1, Bldg 4, Bldg 7).\n    *   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: Multiple banks are shown attached to or immediately adjacent to the buildings (e.g., Bldg 2, Bldg 3, Bldg 5, Bldg 8).\n*   **Underground vs. Overhead lines:** Both are present.\n    *   *Overhead:* As noted above, located along the western (\"-OHE-\") and southern (\"-OHE-\") perimeters.\n    *   *Underground:* A network of solid blue lines connects the proposed buildings, pull boxes, and transformer pads throughout the interior of the site. Two distinct callouts with leader lines explicitly label these as **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: one pointing to the blue line network on the western side of the site near the entrance, and another pointing to the blue line network on the eastern side near Building 4.\n\n**2. Voltage classification and line type:**\n\n*   **Voltage class:** The document does **not** provide specific voltage classifications (e.g., 12.5kV, 138kV) for either the transmission or distribution lines.\n*   **Labels/markings:** The lines are only demarcated by line type labels: **\"-OHE-\"** for overhead electric lines and solid blue lines with periodic **\"E\"** markers denoting the proposed underground electrical routing.\n\n**3. Spatial relationship with proposed buildings:**\n\n*   **Proximity of overhead lines to buildings:**\n    *   *Western \"-OHE-\" line:* Building 1 and Building 8 are the closest structures to this line. Based on the provided scale (1\" = 20'), the distance from the front facades of these buildings to the overhead line appears to be approximately 30 to 40 feet.\n    *   *Southern \"-OHE-\" line:* Building 7 and Building 8 are closest to this line. Based on the scale, the distance appears to be approximately 30 to 40 feet.\n*   **Notes about clearances or setbacks:** There are **no specific notes, dimension lines, or dashed boundaries** on this sheet indicating required safety clearances or structural setbacks specifically related to the electrical lines.\n\n**4. Notes about tree clearances or utility compatibility:**\n\n*   **Tree planting restrictions:** There are **no notes or symbols** indicating restrictions on tree planting near utilities. The plan shows existing/proposed tree canopies (large circles) overlapping significantly with the proposed blue underground electrical lines in several areas (e.g., north of Bldg 1, around Bldg 3, east of Bldg 4).\n*   **Austin Energy approvals:** Despite the project being located in Austin, Texas (as noted in the title block), there are **no references, notes, stamps, or conditions** mentioning \"Austin Energy\" on this specific sheet.\n\n*(Note regarding Utility Notes: The \"Utility Notes\" section in the bottom right corner contains four items, but they are general contractor instructions regarding verifying locations (e.g., \"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\") and do not specify clearances or tree compatibility.)*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1557,"outputTokens":997,"totalTokens":4426,"reasoningTokens":1872},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the electrical design plan on Sheet 21 and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. The location and nature of all electric utility infrastructure shown:\n   - Are there overhead electric lines on the property? If yes, where are they located?\n   - Are there utility poles shown on the site plan? If yes, how many and where?\n   - Are there pad-mounte