nd:* A network of solid blue lines connects the proposed buildings, pull boxes, and transformer pads throughout the interior of the site. Two distinct callouts with leader lines explicitly label these as **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: one pointing to the blue line network on the western side of the site near the entrance, and another pointing to the blue line network on the eastern side near Building 4.\n\n**2. Voltage classification and line type:**\n\n*   **Voltage class:** The document does **not** provide specific voltage classifications (e.g., 12.5kV, 138kV) for either the transmission or distribution lines.\n*   **Labels/markings:** The lines are only demarcated by line type labels: **\"-OHE-\"** for overhead electric lines and solid blue lines with periodic **\"E\"** markers denoting the proposed underground electrical routing.\n\n**3. Spatial relationship with proposed buildings:**\n\n*   **Proximity of overhead lines to buildings:**\n    *   *Western \"-OHE-\" line:* Building 1 and Building 8 are the closest structures to this line. Based on the provided scale (1\" = 20'), the distance from the front facades of these buildings to the overhead line appears to be approximately 30 to 40 feet.\n    *   *Southern \"-OHE-\" line:* Building 7 and Building 8 are closest to this line. Based on the scale, the distance appears to be approximately 30 to 40 feet.\n*   **Notes about clearances or setbacks:** There are **no specific notes, dimension lines, or dashed boundaries** on this sheet indicating required safety clearances or structural setbacks specifically related to the electrical lines.\n\n**4. Notes about tree clearances or utility compatibility:**\n\n*   **Tree planting restrictions:** There are **no notes or symbols** indicating restrictions on tree planting near utilities. The plan shows existing/proposed tree canopies (large circles) overlapping significantly with the proposed blue underground electrical lines in several areas (e.g., north of Bldg 1, around Bldg 3, east of Bldg 4).\n*   **Austin Energy approvals:** Despite the project being located in Austin, Texas (as noted in the title block), there are **no references, notes, stamps, or conditions** mentioning \"Austin Energy\" on this specific sheet.\n\n*(Note regarding Utility Notes: The \"Utility Notes\" section in the bottom right corner contains four items, but they are general contractor instructions regarding verifying locations (e.g., \"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\") and do not specify clearances or tree compatibility.)*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1557,"outputTokens":997,"totalTokens":4426,"reasoningTokens":1872},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":572879.8148,"endTime":601337.515614,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"i2fqacGmDsmn8eEPstGEkAw"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.037542","marketCost":"0.037542","inferenceCost":"0.037542","inputInferenceCost":"0.003114","outputInferenceCost":"0.034428","generationId":"gen_01KPXT8XQPWMV7TYE3V0GM