xt \"LOC\"): Label reads **\"PL M\"**\n*   Tree located near the top-right corner of the building: Label reads **\"PL M\"**\n\n**Eastern Edge (Right side):**\n*   One tree circle is located immediately to the right of the shaded area labeled \"FILTRATION BASIN\". Label reads **\"M\"**\n\n**Southern Edge (Bottom side, concentrated in the bottom-right corner):**\n*   There is a cluster of four tree circles near the bottom right property corner.\n    *   Tree closest to the bottom property line, furthest left in the cluster: Label reads **\"M\"**\n    *   Tree slightly above and to the right of the previous one: Label reads **\"M\"**\n    *   Tree near the actual bottom-right corner point: Label reads **\"M\"**\n    *   Tree slightly above the corner point: Label reads **\"M\"**\n\n***\n\n### 3) Tree Locations Near Transformer Pads\n\n*   Based strictly on the provided Sheet 28, **there are no visible labels or symbols explicitly designating \"Transformer,\" \"Pad,\" or \"Elec Pad.\"**\n*   While there are utility lines indicated (e.g., \"OHE\" for overhead electric along the bottom edge, \"SD\" for storm drain, \"LOC\" for limits of construction), the specific concrete equipment pads usually associated with transformers are not drawn or labeled on this landscape plan.\n*   Because Sheet 21 is not available for cross-referencing in this view, I cannot determine which of the trees listed above are near transformer locations.\n\n***\n\n### 4) Cross-Referencing Legend: Species Codes, Caliper Sizes, and Utility Compatibility\n\nThere is no specific \"Plant Schedule\" or table listing botanical species (e.g., Oak, Elm) on this sheet. The labels found inside the tree symbols (\"SY\", \"PL\", \"M\") refer to usage categories rather than specific botanical species codes.\n\nDirectly below the \"KEY NOTES\" section on the right side of the document, the following exact text defines these category codes:\n\n> **SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n> **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n> **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n> **M** - MITIGATION TREE\n\n**Addressing specific requirements based on the available text:**\n\n*   **Tree Species Types & Codes:** Specific tree species (botanical names) and specific species codes (e.g., \"QV\" for Quercus virginiana) are **not present** on this sheet. The codes shown denote the tree's purpose on the site (Street Yard, Parking Lot, Mitigation).\n*   **Caliper Sizes:** The legend notes that \"SY\" and \"PL\" trees are in **\"EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH\"**. No specific installation caliper sizes (e.g., 2\", 3\", 4\") are defined for any individual tree on this page.\n*   **Utility-Compatible Species:** There are **no notes or designations** within the legend, key notes, or irrigation notes on this sheet that identify which trees are \"utility-compatible.\""}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8749633-cddc-4008-9f86-e2f0ef414315","uuid":"fc2f6c79-107c-4b5b-b218-8b5b14de3646","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the detailed information requested regarding trees, labels, and site features.\n\n### 1 & 2) Location of Trees and Visible Labels/Call-outs\n\nThe trees on this plan are represented by distinct circular symbols with a crosshair or dot in the center. Inside or directly adjacent to these circles are category codes. Note: The plan also shows irregular, wavy outlines representing existing tree canopies, primarily along the eastern and southern property lines, but these do not have individual species or category labels attached to them in the same manner.\n\nHere is the location of every proposed tree symbol (perfect circles) and its exact corresponding label:\n\n**Western Edge (Left side, along the curved shaded paving area):**\n*   Three large tree circles are spaced along the far left edge within the shaded area.\n    * 