{"level":30,"time":1776969886471,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01E15i9Xm63kiKvXNfbc1cMJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F4fvmnEUwvtityhaounbUW","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"This landscape plan mentions overhead electric (OHE) utility lines. Please examine the drawing carefully and identify: (1) Where are the overhead electric lines located relative to the site? (2) Do they run across the property, along property boundaries, or adjacent to the site on Valley View Road or adjacent properties? (3) What is their proximity to buildings, trees, and other site features? (4) Are there dimension annotations showing clearances from the overhead lines to buildings or landscape features? Please describe the exact locations of any OHE lines shown."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1705,"cache_read_input_tokens":58095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1705},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a582675-f45b-4e40-ac49-d1379f357a0d","uuid":"e12485ed-099b-4073-9296-4d8187152710"}
{"level":30,"time":1776969886472,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"This landscape plan mentions overhead electric (OHE) utility lines. Please examine the drawing carefully and identify: (1) Where are the overhead electric lines located relative to the site? (2) Do they run across the property, along property boundaries, or adjacent to the site on Valley View Road or adjacent properties? (3) What is their proximity to buildings, trees, and other site features? (4) Are there dimension annotations showing clearances from the overhead lines to buildings or landscape features? Please describe the exact locations of any OHE lines shown.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776969889432,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01S9vrAtoXhj89nn7hAmZopZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The search didn't return specific tree clearance comments, only the references to UCM sections. This suggests the detailed comments are likely in the Bluebeam document which I can't access.\n\nLet me now use my knowledge of ECM Appendix F to evaluate the tree species. From the grouping guidance and my understanding of Austin's tree requirements:\n\n**Trees proposed for planting:**\n1. **Live Oak (Quercus virginiana)** - 2 trees, 100 GAL, 4\" CAL\n2. **Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia)** - 10 trees, 100 GAL, 4\" CAL\n3. **Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora)** - 2 trees, 45 GAL, 2.5\" CAL\n4. **Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana)** - 6 trees, 45 GAL, 2.5\" CAL\n\nAccording to ECM Appendix F (which I know from the context):\n- **Live Oak**: Mature height ~50 feet - LARGE TREE, typically UC (utility-compatible)\n- **Cedar Elm**: Mature height ~50-60 feet - LARGE TREE, typically UC (utility-compatible)\n- **Texas Mountain Laurel**: Mature height ~20-25 feet - typically UC (utility-compatible)\n- **Mexican Redbud**: Mature height ~30 feet - NOT UC, but under 40 feet\n\nNow, based on the vision analysis of the landscape plan:\n- Trees are planted along the southern boundary of the property where there is an OHE (overhead electric) line\n- The distance appears to be 0-10 feet from the OHE line based on the scale\n\nThis is a critical issue because:\n1. **EL-2.1**: Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution - if Mexican Redbud is not UC, this could be a violation\n\n\n2. **EL-2.3**: Large trees (40+ feet) within 25 feet of distribution - Live Oak and Cedar Elm are large trees potentially within this zone\n3. **EL-2.14**: Trees not shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric - the landscape plan does show OHE but doesn't label specific tree species or clearances\n4. **EL-2.10**: Plant legend/species identification - need to verify species are clearly identified on landscape plan\n\nI need to examine the landscape plan more closely to confirm whether individual tree species are labeled and if clearance distances are documented.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":544,"cache_read_input_tokens":58981,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":544},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"970d0b0f-6cb0-49b0-933a-a570c2e8fa2d","uuid":"5cbee831-0765-45f9-8314-a079dbe051ac"}
