{"level":30,"time":1776969895608,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01L3DHT755tESnyWSPtUt8BP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BQ9EVXxYGvFzZrZgRdL2WM","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the SOUTHERN BOUNDARY of Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan), where the overhead electric (OHE) line runs. \n\nPlease provide:\n\n1. **Tree Count and Positions:** Count the individual tree symbols (circles) plotted along or very near (within ~15-20 feet of) the OHE line. Describe their positions from west to east.\n\n2. **Tree Labels/Symbols:** For each tree near the OHE line, identify any label text next to it, such as:\n   - SY (Street Yard Tree)\n   - PL (Parking Lot Tree)\n   - M (Mitigation Tree)\n   - P (Parking Buffer Point Tree)\n   - Or species names/abbreviations if visible\n\n3. **Distance Estimates:** For each tree, estimate its horizontal distance from the OHE line based on the scale (1\" = 20'):\n   - Within 5 feet\n   - 5-10 feet\n   - 10-15 feet\n   - 15-25 feet\n   - >25 feet\n\n4. **Clarity for Review:** Can the specific species of trees near the OHE line be determined from Sheet 31 alone, or must the viewer reference Sheet 35 (plant schedule) to match symbols to species names?\n\nContext: The regulatory requirement mandates that utility-compatible trees remain 15+ feet from distribution conductors, and large trees (≥40 ft mature height) remain 25+ feet. Identification of both distance and species is necessary to assess compliance."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1602,"cache_read_input_tokens":62936,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1602},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2af985ee-646f-4363-9e8d-5974ccc4a371","uuid":"9c920d22-91e8-427c-9deb-0d32cc021b9f"}
{"level":30,"time":1776969895609,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the SOUTHERN BOUNDARY of Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan), where the overhead electric (OHE) line runs. \n\nPlease provide:\n\n1. **Tree Count and Positions:** Count the individual tree symbols (circles) plotted along or very near (within ~15-20 feet of) the OHE line. Describe their positions from west to east.\n\n2. **Tree Labels/Symbols:** For each tree near the OHE line, identify any label text next to it, such as:\n   - SY (Street Yard Tree)\n   - PL (Parking Lot Tree)\n   - M (Mitigation Tree)\n   - P (Parking Buffer Point Tree)\n   - Or species names/abbreviations if visible\n\n3. **Distance Estimates:** For each tree, estimate its horizontal distance from the OHE line based on the scale (1\" = 20'):\n   - Within 5 feet\n   - 5-10 feet\n   - 10-15 feet\n   - 15-25 feet\n   - >25 feet\n\n4. **Clarity for Review:** Can the specific species of trees near the OHE line be determined from Sheet 31 alone, or must the viewer reference Sheet 35 (plant schedule) to match symbols to species names?\n\nContext: The regulatory requirement mandates that utility-compatible trees remain 15+ feet from distribution conductors, and large trees (≥40 ft mature height) remain 25+ feet. Identification of both distance and species is necessary to assess compliance.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776969907733,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the Site Plan for transformer pad locations and clearances. Please provide:\n\n1. Are transformer pads shown on this site plan? If so, describe their locations relative to buildings and parking areas.\n2. Are there parking spaces immediately adjacent to any transformer locations? If so, which transformers?\n3. Are there dumpsters, driveway edges, or vehicle circulation areas near transformer locations?\n4. Are there sidewalks, curbs, or walkways near the transformer locations?\n5. Are any landscape features (trees, shrubs) visible near transformer locations?\n6. Are fire lanes or emergency vehicle routes shown? If so, how do they relate to transformer locations?\n7. Are there retaining walls on the site, and if so, are any near transformer locations?\n8. What is the distance from each transformer pad to the nearest building edge (use visual estimate if no dimensions are shown)?\n9. Are there utility easements shown relative to transformer locations?\n10. Are transformer pads located near property boundaries or easement lines?\n\nUse compass directions (NE, SW, center, etc.) and building references for clarity.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided site plan, here are the details regarding the transformer pad locations and clearances:\n\n**1. Are transformer pads shown on this site plan? If so, describe their locations relative to buildings and parking areas.**\n*   Yes, one transformer pad is explicitly labeled on the plan as \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\".\n*   **Location:** It is located on the central-western side of the site. It sits along the inner (eastern) edge of the main north-south internal driveway.\n*   **Relative to buildings:** It is positioned to the west of the open space/walkway area between \"**Bldg. 1**\" (near Unit 101) and \"**Bldg. 8**\" (near Unit 801).\n*   **Relative to parking:** It is not located in or immediately adjacent to the main parking clusters. The nearest marked parking spaces are located further north (west of Bldg. 1) and south (south of Bldg. 8).\n\n**2. Are there parking spaces immediately adjacent to any transformer locations? If so, which transformers?**\n*   No. There are no striped parking spaces immediately adjacent to the labeled \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\".\n\n**3. Are there dumpsters, driveway edges, or vehicle circulation areas near transformer locations?**\n*   **Dumpsters:** No dumpsters or trash enclosures are explicitly labeled near the transformer pad.\n*   **Driveway edges/vehicle circulation:** Yes. The transformer pad is situated immediately adjacent to the eastern curb/edge of the main north-south internal driveway (vehicle circulation aisle) on the western side of the property.\n\n**4. Are there sidewalks, curbs, or walkways near the transformer locations?**\n*   Yes. The pad is adjacent to the driveway curb.\n*   Immediately to the east of the pad is an area labeled \"**Tree Well / need to look up approp. detail**\". From this tree well area, a walkway labeled \"**Construct 4' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ) See Dtl 432S-1**\" leads eastward between Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 8.\n*   Across the driveway to the west, there is a sidewalk labeled \"**Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 432S-1**\".\n\n**5. Are any landscape features (trees, shrubs) visible near transformer locations?**\n*   Yes. The pad is located immediately adjacent to (just west of) a rectangular area specifically labeled \"**Tree Well**\".\n*   Additionally, circular symbols indicating existing trees (irregular scalloped outlines) are shown slightly to the south and west of the pad along the driveway.\n\n**6. Are fire lanes or emergency vehicle routes shown? If so, how do they relate to transformer locations?**\n*   While the main internal driveway looping the site is typical for emergency access, there is no explicit \"**Fire Lane**\" text, striping, or hatching labeled immediately adjacent to the transformer pad on this specific document. The pad borders the standard vehicle circulation driveway.\n\n**7. Are there retaining walls on the site, and if so, are any near transformer locations?**\n*   Yes, there are several retaining walls on the site, explicitly labeled with texts such as \"**Begin Concrete Retaining Wall**\", \"**End Concrete Retaining Wall**\", and \"**Concrete Retaining Wall**\" (primarily located along the northern, eastern, and southern perimeter boundaries).\n*   **No**, there are no retaining walls visible near the labeled \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\" on the western side of the site.\n\n**8. What is the distance from each transformer pad to the nearest building edge (use visual estimate if no dimensions are shown)?**\n*   There are no explicit dimension lines indicating the distance from the pad to the buildings.\n*   Based on the provided graphic scale (\"**Scale 1\" = 20'**\"), the visual estimate from the eastern edge of the transformer pad to the nearest western edges of **Bldg. 1** and **Bldg. 8** is approximately 30 to 40 feet.\n\n**9. Are there utility easements shown relative to transformer locations?**\n*   Yes. Just north of the transformer pad along the driveway, there is a boundary labeled \"**Sidewalk Easement Tract**\".\n*   Underground utility lines (dashed lines labeled \"**W**\" for water, \"**WW**\" for wastewater, and \"**SD**\" for storm drain) are shown crossing or running parallel to the driveway in the general vicinity.\n*   A \"**10' P.U.E.**\" (Public Utility Easement) is shown running parallel to the western property boundary, located across the driveway from the pad.\n\n**10. Are transformer pads located near property boundaries or easement lines?**\n*   The transformer pad is located in the western portion of the site, relatively near the main western property boundary, but it is buffered from the actual property line by the internal driveway, a sidewalk, and a strip of land containing the \"**10' P.U.E.**\".\n*   It is located very close to the internal \"**Sidewalk Easement Tract**\" located just to its north.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1540,"outputTokens":1119,"totalTokens":5185,"reasoningTokens":2526},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Site Plan for transformer pad locations and clearances. Please provide:\n\n1. Are transformer pads shown on this site plan? If so, describ