m the actual property line by the internal driveway, a sidewalk, and a strip of land containing the \"**10' P.U.E.**\".\n*   It is located very close to the internal \"**Sidewalk Easement Tract**\" located just to its north."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776969910344,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Sheet 21 is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan. I need detailed analysis of the transformer pad locations in relation to adjacent features, particularly:\n\n1. TRANSFORMER PAD TO PARKING PROXIMITY: For each of the 5 transformer pads visible on this sheet:\n   - Identify its location (by building number and direction)\n   - Measure the visual distance from the transformer pad symbol to the nearest parking space edge\n   - Is the transformer pad drawn as part of or immediately adjacent to the parking area?\n   - Estimate if any transformer pad appears to be within 4 feet of parking areas\n   - Are there any bollards or protective barriers drawn around any transformer pads?\n\n2. TRANSFORMER PAD TO BUILDING PROXIMITY:\n   - For each transformer, what is the visual distance to the nearest building wall?\n   - Are clearance dimensions shown?\n\n3. TRANSFORMER PAD DETAILS:\n   - Can you see access door orientation marked on any pad symbols?\n   - Are any pads in confined spaces or notched building areas?\n   - Do any appear to be in easement areas that are marked?\n\n4. SCALE CONFIRMATION: Confirm the scale is 1\" = 20' and describe how this relates to the visual distances observed.\n\nPlease be very specific about measurements based on the visual layout of the parking areas relative to each transformer pad symbol.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided document (Sheet 21, Preliminary Electrical Design Plan), here is the information regarding the transformer pad locations and specific requirements requested:\n\n### 1. TRANSFORMER PAD TO PARKING PROXIMITY\n\n*Note: On this specific electrical plan layer, standard striped parking spaces are not explicitly drawn. Drive aisles, curbs, and unit driveways are visible. Proximity is evaluated based on the nearest paved drive aisle/curb.*\n\n**Pad 1:**\n*   **Location:** Upper left side of the sheet, West of **Bldg. 1** near the curved entrance drive. Look for the callout box **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Visual Distance to Paving:** The pad symbol is located within a landscaped island area surrounded by curbing. Visually, the edge of the pad is very close to the back of the curb line.\n*   **Adjacent to Parking:** It is not part of a striped parking area, but it is immediately adjacent to the curb of the main entry drive aisle.\n*   **Within 4 feet:** Based on the scale, the visual gap between the pad symbol and the curb line is extremely small, suggesting it is highly likely within 4 feet of the paved surface/curb.\n*   **Bollards:** There are no symbols (typically small circles) indicating bollards or protective barriers drawn around this pad.\n\n**Pad 2:**\n*   **Location:** Middle left side of the sheet, West of **Bldg. 2**. Look for the callout box **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Visual Distance to Paving:** The pad is located west of the drive aisle, sitting behind a line indicating a sidewalk.\n*   **Adjacent to Parking:** It is not adjacent to parking. It is separated from the main drive aisle by a sidewalk and a narrow strip of land.\n*   **Within 4 feet:** Because the sidewalk sits between the pad and the curb, it appears to be further than 4 feet from the actual drive aisle paving.\n*   **Bollards:** No bollards or protective barriers are drawn around this pad.\n\n**Pad 3:**\n*   **Location:** Bottom left side of the sheet, West of **Bldg. 8**. Look for the callout box **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Visual Distance to Paving:** Similar to Pad 2, it is located west of the drive aisle, behind the sidewalk line.\n*   **Adjacent to Parking:** It is not adjacent to parking. It is separated from the drive aisle by the sidewalk.\n*   **Within 4 feet:** Due to the sidewalk separation, it visually appears to be more than 4 feet away from the drive aisle paving.\n*   **Bollards:** No bollards or protective barriers are drawn around this pad.\n\n**Pad 4:**\n*   **Location:** Bottom center of the sheet, East of **Bldg. 7** (between Bldg. 7 and the eastern property line). Look for the callout box **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Visual Distance to Paving:** There is no drive aisle or parking area shown on this side of the building. The pad sits in a grassy/corridor area.\n*   **Adjacent to Parking:** No.\n*   **Within 4 feet:** No parking or paving is nearby.\n*   **Bollards:** No bollards or protective barriers are drawn around this pad.\n\n**Pad 5:**\n*   **Location:** Middle right side of the sheet, East of **Bldg. 4**. Look for the callout box **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Visual Distance to Paving:** Similar to Pad 4, there is no drive aisle or parking area shown on this side of the building.\n*   **Adjacent to Parking:** No.\n*   **Within 4 feet:** No parking or paving is nearby.\n*   **Bollards:** No bollards or protective barriers are drawn around this pad.\n\n### 2. TRANSFORMER PAD TO BUILDING PROXIMITY\n\n*   **Pad 1 (West of Bldg 1):** The entrance drive aisle completely separates the pad from the building. Visually, this is a significant distance (well over 20 feet).\n*   **Pad 2 (West of Bldg 2):** The pad is separated from the western wall of the building by what appears to be a landscape strip and walkway. Based on scale, the visual gap represents roughly 10 to 15 feet.\n*   **Pad 3 (West of Bldg 8):** Similar to Pad 2, it is separated from the western wall of Bldg 8. The visual gap represents roughly 10 to 15 feet.\n*   **Pad 4 (East of Bldg 7):** Sits in the corridor between the building and the eastern property line. The visual distance to the eastern wall of Bldg 7 appears to be roughly 10 to 15 feet.\n*   **Pad 5 (East of Bldg 4):** Sits in the corridor between the building and the eastern property line. The visual distance to the eastern wall of Bldg 4 appears to be roughly 10 to 15 feet.\n*   **Clearance dimensions:** There are **no** specific numerical clearance dimensions (e.g., lines with measurements like `<-- 10' -->`) drawn between any of the transformer pads and the adjacent buildings on this sheet.\n\n### 3. TRANSFORMER PAD DETAILS\n\n*   **Access door orientation:** The transformer pad symbols are drawn as simple, empty squares/rectangles. There are **no markings, arrows, or distinct line types** on any of the five symbols indicating which direction the access doors face.\n*   **Confined spaces or notched areas:** None of the pads are drawn inside confined spaces (like enclosed courtyards) or notched into the footprint of the buildings. Pads 1, 2, and 3 are in open areas near the front. Pads 4 and 5 are in the open, straight corridor space between the backs of the buildings and the eastern property line.\n*   **Easement areas:**\n    *   Pad 1 sits within a complex web of dashed lines near the front property boundary, placing it within or immediately adjacent to front utility/wastewater easements.\n    *   Pads 2 and 3 sit just outside a dashed line labeled **\"Sidewalk Easement Doc#\"**.\n    *   Pads 4 and 5 sit near, but appear to be just outside of, a dashed boundary on the east labeled **\"25' Drainage Easement...\"**.\n    *   No specific, individual square easement boxes are drawn perfectly outlining the footprint of the individual pads themselves.\n\n### 4. SCALE CONFIRMATION\n\n*   **Scale Confirmation:** The top right corner of the document features a graphic scale bar with the exact text: **Scale 1\" = 20'**.\n*   **Relation to Visual Distances:** This scale dictates that every 1 physical inch measured on the printed plan at 100% size equals 20 real-world feet. Consequently, visual distances that appear quite small on the page represent significant gaps. For example, a standard 6-foot wide transformer pad would appear as roughly slightly larger than 1/4 inch on the paper. Because objects like the pads and curbs are drawn distinctly apart (even if the gap is only a millimeter or two visually), this confirms a separation of several feet in reality. Conversely, where Pad 1 touches the curb line almost exactly, it signifies the pad is likely situated right at the edge of the pavement.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1596,"outputTokens":1618,"totalTokens":6024,"reasoningTokens":2810},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Sheet 21 is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan. I need detailed analysi