{"level":30,"time":1776969913710,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HHeg3z3ZqM6Gf9ksPgqbAG","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n     2→\n     3→Site plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n    11→* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    12→* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    13→* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    14→* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    15→* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n    16→* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n    17→* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n    18→* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n    19→* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n    20→* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n    21→* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n    22→* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    23→* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    26→\n    27→* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    28→  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n    29→  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n    30→\n    31→* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n    32→  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n    33→  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n    34→\n    35→* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n    36→  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n    37→  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n    38→\n    39→* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n    40→  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n    41→  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n    42→\n    43→* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n    44→  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n    45→  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n    46→\n    47→* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n    48→  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n    49→  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n    50→\n    51→* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    52→  Provides surveyor reference points.\n    53→  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n    54→\n    55→* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n    56→  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n    57→  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n    58→\n    59→* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    60→  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n    61→  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n    62→\n    63→---\n    64→\n    65→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    66→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b5611a6-cdc1-4cee-bcc8-9d8730c6403f","uuid":"7361bcf8-c82e-4c6b-aa18-e0b46d98e9d7","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 10 — Fire Protection Plan\n\nSite plan illustrating fire lanes, hydrants, and fire zone details.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Fire Protection Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's fire access routing, fire lane markings, fire hydrant locations, and necessary suppression system requirements to ensure compliance with the City of Austin Fire Code and NFPA standards. \n\n**Key values**:\n* Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50'\n* Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0'\n* Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0'\n* Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50'\n* Total private fire hydrants on site: 1\n* Required fire suppression system: NFPA 13D for all buildings\n* Fire Zone curb stenciling: 4-inch high white letters at 30-foot intervals on painted red curbs\n* Fire Zone signage dimensions: 305 mm x 457 mm overall, with 38 mm to 76.2 mm lettering heights\n* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n  Contains the detailed site layout showing buildings 1-8, fire lanes, fire hydrants, walls, fences, and utility easements.\n  Use VISION for spatial layout of fire access routing, hydrant placement, and building footprints.\n\n* **Block 11: notes — Fire Zone Notes**\n  Contains rules for fire zone demarcation, including standard detail references and curb painting instructions.\n  READ for exact specifications on signage placement, red curb painting with 4-inch stenciling, and the requirement that all private hydrants must be painted red.\n\n* **Block 9: notes — General System Notes**\n  Contains requirements for underground main installation and testing for sprinkler systems.\n  READ for exact testing specifications (NFPA 13 and NFPA 24) and the required Knox-box location at the exterior fire riser room doors.\n\n* **Block 7: notes — Private Hydrant Note**\n  Details the City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility requirements regarding the site's hydrants.\n  READ to confirm the presence of 1 private hydrant and the owner's legal obligation for annual service and flow testing.\n\n* **Block 3: notes — Fire Riser Room Note**\n  Specifies the required internal fire suppression system.\n  READ to confirm the NFPA 13D system requirement for all proposed buildings.\n\n* **Block 1: diagram — Fire Zone Signage Detail**\n  Contains City of Austin Standard Detail 901S-6 for \"NO PARKING FIRE ZONE TOW-AWAY ZONE\" signs.\n  READ for exact values of sign dimensions, letter heights, and material colors (red transparent over silver reflective background), and use VISION for the visual layout of the sign text.\n\n* **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n  Provides surveyor reference points.\n  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n\n* **Blocks 6, 8: notes — Sheet Cross-References**\n  Brief notes pointing the reviewer to other sheets for additional data.\n  READ to locate the Tree List (Sheet 32) and the Fire Flow Test results (Sheet 18).\n\n* **Blocks 5, 10, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n  Contains the title block, legal description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision), Texas 811 callout, and standard disclaimers regarding existing utilities and engineer responsibility.\n  READ for general project information and administrative records.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776969913973,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Examine the existing conditions survey and identify all overhead utility features. Specifically look for:\n1. Overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) - show where they are located relative to the property boundary\n2. Utility poles - note their locations and any associated guy wires\n3. The southern boundary area near Valley View Road - are there overhead lines there?\n4. Any proximity of overhead lines to the property being developed\n5. Easement boundaries - where are the electric easements located?\n\nDescribe the specific locations and relationships you see.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Boundary, Improvements, Topographic & Tree Survey\" document, here are the findings regarding overhead utility features and easements. \n\n*Note on Orientation: The North arrow on this drawing points to the **left**. Therefore, Valley View Road (on the left of the page) is geographically to the North. However, for clarity in describing the visual layout, I will use page-relative directions (top, bottom, left, right) alongside the surveyor bearings.*\n\nHere is the analysis of the requested items:\n\n### 1. Overhead Utility Lines (O.H.U.L.) Locations\n*   **Bottom Boundary Area (Bearing \"N63°30'57\"W 414.24'\")**: A distinct dashed line labeled **\"- O.H.U.L. -\"** runs parallel to this bottom boundary. For the majority of its length, this line is located just *outside* the property boundary, traversing the adjacent property to the \"south\" (bottom of page, geographically East). \n*   **Crossing the Boundary**: As the \"- O.H.U.L. -\" line approaches Valley View Road (left side of the page), it crosses over the property boundary line, entering the southwest (bottom-left) corner of the developed site to connect to a utility pole.\n*   **Valley View Road (Left Boundary, Bearing \"N28°04'28\"E\")**: Overhead lines appear to run along the right-of-way of Valley View Road, connecting the utility poles situated at the property corners along the road.\n\n### 2. Utility Poles and Associated Guy Wires\nThere are several utility poles marked with the standard circle-and-cross symbol. \n*   **Pole 1 (Bottom-Left Corner)**: Located near the intersection of Valley View Road and the bottom boundary (\"N63°30'57\"W\"). This pole connects to the \"- O.H.U.L. -\" running along the bottom boundary. It features a guy wire extending outwards, roughly perpendicular to the road.\n*   **Pole 2 (Top-Left Corner)**: Located just outside the property boundary near the intersection of Valley View Road and the top boundary (\"S63°02'28\"E\"). This pole has a guy wire that extends inwards, running parallel to the top boundary line.\n*   **Pole 3 (Bottom-Right Area)**: Located off-site, near the rightmost end of the bottom boundary line, anchoring the eastern end of the \"- O.H.U.L. -\" run.\n\n### 3. \"Southern Boundary\" Area Near Valley View Road\nAssuming \"Southern boundary\" refers to the bottom boundary line on the page (bearing \"N63°30'57\"W\") that intersects with Valley View Road:\n*   **Yes, there are overhead lines there.** As noted above, an \"- O.H.U.L. -\" runs closely parallel to this boundary line. While mostly located on the adjacent lot, the line physically crosses over the property corner right at the intersection with Valley View Road to terminate at the utility pole located there.\n\n### 4. Proximity of Overhead Lines to the Property\n*   The primary overhead line along the bottom boundary is in **extreme proximity** to the property being developed. It runs parallel just a few feet outside the boundary line for most of its length and physically encroaches over the property line at the bottom-left corner near the road. \n*   The interior of the property, specifically where the proposed main building footprint (labeled **\"SLAB F.F.E.=686.8'\"**) is located, appears clear of any bisecting overhead utility lines.\n\n### 5. Easement Boundaries\nThere are specific electrical and public utility easements designated parallel to the property boundaries:\n*   **Bottom Boundary Easement**: There is a dashed line running parallel just inside the bottom property line (\"N63°30'57\"W\"). A leader line originating from the right side of the drawing points to this area, labeling it exactly as: **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 5419, PG. 583 P.R.T.C.TX\"**. \n*   **Top Boundary Easement**: Similarly, there is a dashed line running parallel just inside the top property line (\"S63°02'28\"E\"). The text labeling this area reads exactly: **\"5' P.U.E. VOL. 5419, PG. 583 P.R.T.C.TX\"** (P.U.E. stands for Public Utility Easement, which typically encompasses electrical lines).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1423,"outputTokens":1002,"totalTokens":7332,"reasoningTokens":4907},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the existing conditions survey and identify all overhead utility features. Specifically look for:\n1. Overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) - show where they are located relative to the property boundary\n2. Utility poles - note their locations and any associated guy wires\n3. The southern boundary area near Valley View Road - are there overhead lines there?\n4. Any proximity of overhead lines to the property being developed\n5. Easement boundaries - where are the electric easements located?\n\nDescribe the specific locations and relationships you see."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-Eywt6JAomxi3gv8Rp844zKw3","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 18:45:13 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-route