 the **left**. Therefore, Valley View Road (on the left of the page) is geographically to the North. However, for clarity in describing the visual layout, I will use page-relative directions (top, bottom, left, right) alongside the surveyor bearings.*\n\nHere is the analysis of the requested items:\n\n### 1. Overhead Utility Lines (O.H.U.L.) Locations\n*   **Bottom Boundary Area (Bearing \"N63°30'57\"W 414.24'\")**: A distinct dashed line labeled **\"- O.H.U.L. -\"** runs parallel to this bottom boundary. For the majority of its length, this line is located just *outside* the property boundary, traversing the adjacent property to the \"south\" (bottom of page, geographically East). \n*   **Crossing the Boundary**: As the \"- O.H.U.L. -\" line approaches Valley View Road (left side of the page), it crosses over the property boundary line, entering the southwest (bottom-left) corner of the developed site to connect to a utility pole.\n*   **Valley View Road (Left Boundary, Bearing \"N28°04'28\"E\")**: Overhead lines appear to run along the right-of-way of Valley View Road, connecting the utility poles situated at the property corners along the road.\n\n### 2. Utility Poles and Associated Guy Wires\nThere are several utility poles marked with the standard circle-and-cross symbol. \n*   **Pole 1 (Bottom-Left Corner)**: Located near the intersection of Valley View Road and the bottom boundary (\"N63°30'57\"W\"). This pole connects to the \"- O.H.U.L. -\" running along the bottom boundary. It features a guy wire extending outwards, roughly perpendicular to the road.\n*   **Pole 2 (Top-Left Corner)**: Located just outside the property boundary near the intersection of Valley View Road and the top boundary (\"S63°02'28\"E\"). This pole has a guy wire that extends inwards, running parallel to the top boundary line.\n*   **Pole 3 (Bottom-Right Area)**: Located off-site, near the rightmost end of the bottom boundary line, anchoring the eastern end of the \"- O.H.U.L. -\" run.\n\n### 3. \"Southern Boundary\" Area Near Valley View Road\nAssuming \"Southern boundary\" refers to the bottom boundary line on the page (bearing \"N63°30'57\"W\") that intersects with Valley View Road:\n*   **Yes, there are overhead lines there.** As noted above, an \"- O.H.U.L. -\" runs closely parallel to this boundary line. While mostly located on the adjacent lot, the line physically crosses over the property corner right at the intersection with Valley View Road to terminate at the utility pole located there.\n\n### 4. Proximity of Overhead Lines to the Property\n*   The primary overhead line along the bottom boundary is in **extreme proximity** to the property being developed. It runs parallel just a few feet outside the boundary line for most of its length and physically encroaches over the property line at the bottom-left corner near the road. \n*   The interior of the property, specifically where the proposed main building footprint (labeled **\"SLAB F.F.E.=686.8'\"**) is located, appears clear of any bisecting overhead utility lines.\n\n### 5. Easement Boundaries\nThere are specific electrical and public utility easements designated parallel to the property boundaries:\n*   **Bottom Boundary Easement**: There is a dashed line running parallel just inside the bottom property line (\"N63°30'57\"W\"). A leader line originating from the right side of the drawing points to this area, labeling it exactly as: **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 5419, PG. 583 P.R.T.C.TX\"**. \n*   **Top Boundary Easement**: Similarly, there is a dashed line running parallel just inside the top property line (\"S63°02'28\"E\"). The text labeling this area reads exactly: **\"5' P.U.E. VOL. 5419, PG. 583 P.R.T.C.TX\"** (P.U.E. stands for Public Utility Easement, which typically encompasses electrical lines).","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"s