: **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 4443, PG. 76 P.R.T.C.TX\"**. (No utility lines are visibly drawn within this specific easement on this plan).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Overhead Utility Poles and Ground Infrastructure\nSeveral power poles and associated infrastructure are located around the perimeter of the site:\n\n*   **Along Valley View Road (Bottom of page):**\n    *   Near the northwest property corner area: A pole is marked and labeled **\"POWER POLE WITH LIGHT\"**.\n    *   Centrally located along the road frontage: A pole is marked and labeled **\"POWER POLE\"**. Adjacent to it is a symbol labeled **\"GUY WIRE\"**.\n    *   Near the southwest property corner area: A pole is marked and labeled **\"POWER POLE\"**.\n    *   Slightly further south of that pole, near the property corner, there is an **\"ELECTRIC BOX\"** and another **\"GUY WIRE\"**.\n*   **Along the Northern Boundary (Top of page):**\n    *   Just outside the northwest property line: A pole symbol is visible with an attached **\"GUY WIRE\"**.\n    *   Midway along the northern property line: A pole is marked and labeled **\"POWER POLE\"**.\n    *   Near the northeast property corner: A pole is marked and labeled **\"POWER POLE\"**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Extent and Routing of Overhead Utility Lines (O.H.U.L.)\nThe routing of the existing overhead lines (shown as dashed lines connecting the poles) is visible in three distinct areas:\n\n*   **Roadway Right-of-Way Routing:**\n    A continuous dashed line labeled **\"- O.H.U.L. -\"** runs roughly parallel to **VALLEY VIEW ROAD** along the bottom of the drawing. It connects the \"POWER POLE WITH LIGHT\" on the left, the central \"POWER POLE\", and the \"POWER POLE\" on the right along the road frontage.\n*   **Property Service Drop (Crossing the site):**\n    From the central \"POWER POLE\" located on Valley View Road, a dashed line labeled **\"- O.H.U.L. -\"** branches off and routes directly into the property. It travels east, crossing completely over the existing main building structure (identified by the label **\"SLAB F.F.E.=686.8'\"**). The line terminates near the inner northeast corner of the building's footprint.\n*   **Northern Boundary Routing:**\n    A utility line runs laterally along the entire northern property boundary (the top edge of the drawing). It connects the pole situated just off-site to the west, the mid-point \"POWER POLE\", and the easternmost \"POWER POLE\". This line appears to be routed within the marked **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT\"** and **\"10' ELEC. EASEMENT\"**.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1366,"outputTokens":977,"totalTokens":4988,"reasoningTokens":2645},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you d