o site benchmarks.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-08/guide.md:44:    *   READ for precise elevation values (678.52' and 681.08') and datum information.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-30/guide.md:26:    Contains the main site plan showing townhome building footprints (Units 101-806), topographic contours, and tree locations. READ for exact building square footages and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs), and use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the buildings relative to the existing trees, property lines, and tree protection fencing.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md:12:*   Water Quality Elevation Provided: 675.65 ft msl\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md:13:*   Top of Biofiltration Media Elevation: 672.00 ft\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md:24:*   Use VISION to examine the spatial layout and relationships between pond elements. READ for specific spot elevations (e.g., Top of Biofiltration Media at 672.00) and pipe specifications (e.g., 24\" HDPE @ 1.35%).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md:38:**Block 6: table — Water Quality Pond Water Surface Elevations**\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md:40:*   READ the block content for exact storage volumes at given elevations and to verify the required vs. provided WQV elevations (675.57 vs 675.65).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md:44:*   READ the block content for peak outflow rates (up to 15.60 cfs) at specific event elevations.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md:11:*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md:16:*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md:33:    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md:34:    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-23/guide.md:33:*   **Block 4:** diagram — Fire hydrant assembly plan and elevation. **VISION** for spatial clearances, layout relative to curb/sidewalks, and bottom connection options.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md:7:This sheet presents the Grading Plan for the Valley View Townhomes multi-family development located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail existing and proposed topography, establish building finished floor elevations (FFEs), map storm drainage infrastructure, and indicate the location of retaining walls and utility easements across the site.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md:11:*   **Benchmark 1**: Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md:12:*   **Benchmark 2**: Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md:26:*   **Block 2**: Main site grading drawing showing the layout of the 8 buildings, proposed/existing contours, retaining walls, storm drainage, and various utility easements. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, specific contour line variations, spot elevations, and the exact placement of infrastructure and adjacent property boundaries.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md:28:*   **Block 3**: Benchmark specifications detailing the exact vertical control points (Mag Nail in Asphalt) for the site. READ for exact baseline elevation data.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/guide.md:27:* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-09/guide.md:58:    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-27/guide.md:16:*   **Internal Drop Requirement:** Elevation changes of >24\" require an internal drop structure\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-27/guide.md:35:    Side elevation view of the grinder pump station. Use VISION to understand the vertical layout of the pumps, 10' min fiberglass well, and lifting chains. READ for specific component sizes (2\" valves, 3\" vent, 12\" concrete fill base).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-27/guide.md:37:    Shows plan and elevation views of standard, U-shaped, and bench inverts. Use VISION for the geometry of the flowlines. READ for specific benching criteria (18\" min for 30\"-36\" pipes) and the 1:12 slope requirement.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/guide.md:22:*   **Block 2**: diagram — Section A-A view showing longitudinal vertical elevation. Use VISION for final grade relationships, concrete pad locations, and support stand configurations.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/guide.md:23:*   **Block 1**: diagram — Section B-B view showing transverse vertical elevation. Use VISION for alternative structural details and vertical clearance perspectives.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md:11:*   **Benchmarks**: BM #1 Elevation = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 Elevation = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md:27:    *Use VISION to trace drainage flow paths, examine the spatial relationship between infrastructure and building footprints, and READ for specific pipe dimensions, slopes, and structure elevations.*\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md:34:    Details the vertical control points used for the site plan, specifying the elevations of BM #1 and BM #2.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md:35:    *READ for exact survey elevation references.*\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md:38:    Defines the line types and symbols used on the drawing, such as existing/proposed contours, spot elevations, and limits of construction. It also notes maximum slopes for ADA ramps and landings.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md:10:*   **Water Surface Elevations (WSEL)**: 100-yr (676.75'), 25-yr (676.57'), 10-yr (676.45'), 2-yr (676.25')\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md:11:*   **Biofiltration Media Elevation**: 672.00'\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md:12:*   **Retaining Wall Top Elevations**: 681.00', 677.25', and 677.50' (outfall)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md:13:*   **Outfall Weir**: 4.5' wide at elevation 675.65'\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md:22:    Cross-sectional profile detailing the pond's left and right concrete retaining walls, pipe inlet, rock flow spreader, rock rip-rap, and biofiltration media elevations.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md:31:    *Navigation*: Use VISION for the structural layout and READ for the exact weir elevation (675.65') relative to the projected storm event water surface elevations.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md:11:* Flowline Elevations: FL 8\" = 674.33', FL In 6\" = 674.42', FL Out 6\" = 674.42'\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md:19:* **Block 1**: drawing — Profile View of Water Line A (Wtr-Ln-A). Shows the vertical alignment of the proposed water line from station 0+00 to 0+75, including the transition from AC to DI pipe, reducers, and the meter vault. Use VISION to examine the pipe slopes and relationship to the existing/proposed ground surfaces, and READ for exact flowline elevations, lengths, and the 52' restraint dimension.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md:22:* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:7:This sheet contains the Addressing Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, illustrating the layout, numbering, and finished floor elevations of the proposed residential buildings. Its primary purpose is to define the unit addressing scheme, building square footages, and spatial relationships between the structures, property boundaries, and existing site features like easements.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:19:*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:20:*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:25:*   **Block 1: drawing** — Main site addressing plan showing the townhome layout, individual unit locations, building dimensions, and property lines. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of buildings, unit addressing sequences, finished floor elevations (FFEs), and locations of surrounding easements and utility infrastructure. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:26:*   **Block 2: notes** — Information regarding the primary elevation control points for the project. READ the block content for the exact benchmark elevations, datum (NAVD 88), and point descriptions.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md:22:* Benchmark 1: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md:23:* Benchmark 2: Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md:53:  READ for exact elevation value