{"level":30,"time":1776969971722,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan in detail and provide specific information about:\n\n1. Are tree species identified on this drawing? If yes, which trees and where?\n2. Are there labels next to individual tree symbols (like \"CE\" for Cedar Elm, \"LO\" for Live Oak, \"TML\" for Texas Mountain Laurel, \"MR\" for Mexican Redbud)?\n3. For trees along the southern boundary near the overhead electric line, are any species labels shown?\n4. Is there a plant schedule legend that shows which tree symbols correspond to which species?\n5. Are the trees along the southern boundary differentiated by size or species?\n6. Any notes or callouts relating to overhead utilities and tree species near them?\n\nFocus specifically on the southern edge of the property where the overhead electric line \"-OHE-\" is shown.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the specific information requested:\n\n**1. Are tree species identified on this drawing? If yes, which trees and where?**\nNo, specific tree species are not identified on this drawing. The labels found inside or next to the tree symbols refer to functional classifications rather than species. The \"KEY NOTES\" section in the top right defines these abbreviations as:\n*   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\n\n**2. Are there labels next to individual tree symbols (like \"CE\" for Cedar Elm, \"LO\" for Live Oak, \"TML\" for Texas Mountain Laurel, \"MR\" for Mexican Redbud)?**\nNo. There are no two-letter or three-letter species abbreviations like \"CE\", \"LO\", \"TML\", or \"MR\" present anywhere on this sheet. The only labels inside the tree symbols are \"SY\", \"PL\", \"M\", or numerical key notes like \"H.1\" or \"H.7\".\n\n**3. For trees along the southern boundary near the overhead electric line, are any species labels shown?**\nNo species labels are shown. Along the southern boundary marked with the \"-OHE-\" (overhead electric) line, there are approximately five proposed tree symbols. Only one of these symbols (located near the southeastern corner) contains a label, which is \"M\" (Mitigation Tree). The others have no text labels inside or immediately next to them.\n\n**4. Is there a plant schedule legend that shows which tree symbols correspond to which species?**\nNo, there is no plant schedule or planting legend on this specific sheet. There is a \"KEY NOTES\" section, but it only maps hatch patterns to site features (like \"PROPOSED PAVING\" or \"SOD\") and defines the general tree category abbreviations (SY, PL, P, M) as noted in question 1.\n\n**5. Are the trees along the southern boundary differentiated by size or species?**\nBased solely on this sheet, they are not differentiated by size or species. The tree symbols drawn along the southern \"-OHE-\" line all use the exact same visual graphic (a circle with a thin intersecting cross). Except for the single \"M\" label denoting a mitigation function, there are no callouts indicating different sizes (e.g., caliper inches, gallon sizes) or varying species for these specific trees.\n\n**6. Any notes or callouts relating to overhead utilities and tree species near them?**\nThere are no notes or callouts regarding tree species near overhead utilities on this page. While the overhead electric line is clearly drafted and labeled \"-OHE-\", the \"IRRIGATION NOTES\" and general \"NOTE\" blocks do not contain any text referencing utilities, clearance requirements, or restrictions on tree species planted under or near the lines.","p