roperty boundaries:\n*   **Eastern Easement:** Just inside the eastern property line, running parallel to the `- OHE -` line, is a dashed boundary line with a leader text stating: **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14\"**.\n*   **Southern Easement:** Just inside the southern property line, running parallel to the `- OHE -` line, is a dashed boundary line with leader text stating: **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14, Vol. 73, Pg. 76 F.R.T.C.Tx.\"**. \n\n*(Note: While the prompt asks for \"transmission\" easements, a 5-foot width and standard \"OHE\" symbology typically indicate standard electrical distribution lines rather than large-scale, high-voltage transmission corridors, which usually require much wider easements).*\n\n### Relationship of Proposed Buildings and Site Features to Overhead Facilities\nThe site features appear to be purposefully designed to avoid encroaching on these 5-foot electric easements. \n\n*   **Proposed Buildings:** \n    *   **Bldg. 6** is the closest structure to the eastern `- OHE -` line and the \"5' Electric Easement\".\n    *   **Bldg. 7** and **Bldg. 8** are the closest structures to the southern `- OHE -` line and the \"5' Elec. Easement\".\n    *   None of these buildings cross the dashed 5-foot easement lines; they are set back further into the interior of the lot.\n*   **Retaining Walls:** Extensive **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** structures are proposed between the buildings and the southern/eastern property boundaries. These walls run parallel to the utility lines. Based on the drawing, the outer edge of these retaining walls appears to align with or sit just outside (north/west of) the dashed 5-foot electric easement boundaries, acting as a physical buffer between the occupied site areas and the utility easements. \n*   **Detention Pond:** A **\"Biofiltration/Detention Pond\"** is located in the northeast corner of the site. While it is near the eastern `- OHE -` line, the pond is contained within a **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"** and **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** that keep the infrastructure separated from the immediate property line and associated electric easements. (There is also a **\"15' Easement\"** and a **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** noted near the pond, but these do not explicitly note \"Electric\").\n*   **Driveways and Parking:** The main parking areas and central drive aisles are located well within the interior and western portions of the site, far from the southern and eastern `- OHE -` lines. The **\"Construct Type III Driveway\"** on the west side passes near the **\"Pole\"** and **\"Guy\"** wire located in the northwest corner, but the driveway footprint does not appear to directly conflict with the base of the pole based on the plan view.\n\n**Summary:** There are overhead electric lines (`- OHE -`, `- OH -`) and associated 5-foot electric easements along the southern and eastern perimeters of the site. No proposed buildings, driveways, or detention ponds appear to be located within these transmission/distribution easement areas. The closest proposed structures are concrete retaining walls, which appear to border the edge of the easements without encroaching into them.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1376,"outputTokens":1019,"totalTokens":5827,"reasoningTokens":3432},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as 