{"level":30,"time":1776970186344,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01R9xLryUXcYAKVoAgPKo33i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PRpaDYiUkmbsx6TgBxCDqD","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__run_measure_distance","input":{"reasoning":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees planted along the southern boundary where an overhead electric (-OHE-) line runs. According to UCM § 1.10.10.4, tree clearances are based on: (1) utility-compatible designation, (2) mature height (40+ feet = large tree), and (3) distance from overhead conductors (15 feet for distribution, 50 feet for transmission). The vision analysis indicated trees are planted very close to the OHE line (0-10 feet estimated). I need to measure the actual distances from tree trunks to the outside conductor to determine if clearances meet the 15-foot minimum for distribution lines or identify which specific trees are within the restricted zone.","applicable_checklist_items":[{"checklist_id":"EL-2.1","checklist_deficiency_text":"Non-utility-compatible trees proposed within 15 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor or equipment"},{"checklist_id":"EL-2.3","checklist_deficiency_text":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) proposed within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor or equipment"},{"checklist_id":"EL-2.6","checklist_deficiency_text":"Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric utility pole"}],"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"objectPairs":[{"objectA":"Proposed tree symbol (circle) at southern boundary, southwestern area near utility pole","objectB":"Overhead electric line (-OHE-) conductor at southwestern corner"},{"objectA":"Proposed tree symbol (circle) at southern boundary, center-south area","objectB":"Overhead electric line (-OHE-) conductor in southern perimeter center"},{"objectA":"Proposed tree symbol (circle) at southern boundary, southeastern area near utility pole","objectB":"Overhead electric line (-OHE-) conductor at southeastern corner"}],"scaleInchesPerFoot":0.05},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1814,"cache_read_input_tokens":68066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1814},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"970d0b0f-6cb0-49b0-933a-a570c2e8fa2d","uuid":"9c2c4316-58f8-400f-a82c-afaedfd5eabc"}
{"level":30,"time":1776970186346,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","tool":"run_measure_distance","command":"npx tsx /Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/workflows/review/scripts/measure-distance.ts --outputPath='/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/output/measure-distance.json' --reasoning='The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees planted along the southern boundary where an overhead electric (-OHE-) line runs. According to UCM § 1.10.10.4, tree clearances are based on: (1) utility-compatible designation, (2) mature height (40+ feet = large tree), and (3) distance from overhead conductors (15 feet for distribution, 50 feet for transmission). The vision analysis indicated trees are planted very close to the OHE line (0-10 feet estimated). I need to measure the actual distances from tree trunks to the outside conductor to determine if clearances meet the 15-foot minimum for distribution lines or identify which specific trees are within the restricted zone.' --applicable_checklist_items='[{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-2.1\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Non-utility-compatible trees proposed within 15 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor or equipment\"},{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-2.3\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) proposed within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor or equipment\"},{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-2.6\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric utility pole\"}]' --documentId='1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777' --sheetNum='31' --objectPairs='[{\"objectA\":\"Proposed tree symbol (circle) at southern boundary, southwestern area near utility pole\",\"objectB\":\"Overhead electric line (-OHE-) conductor at southwestern corner\"},{\"objectA\":\"Proposed tree symbol (circle) at southern boundary, center-south area\",\"objectB\":\"Overhead electric line (-OHE-) conductor in southern perimeter center\"},{\"objectA\":\"Proposed tree symbol (circle) at southern boundary, southeastern area near utility pole\",\"objectB\":\"Overhead electric line (-OHE-) conductor at southeastern corner\"}]' --scaleInchesPerFoot='0.05'","msg":"Executing typed script tool"}
{"level":30,"time":1776970482268,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01SwbKVvNB86TakpPzKvqcLL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me understand the key findings so far:\n\nFrom the grouping file (EL-2.md), I need to evaluate tree placement requirements near overhead electric lines. The key requirements are:\n- Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution lines\n- Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 ft of transmission lines\n- Large trees (40+ ft) within 25 ft of distribution lines\n- Large trees (40+ ft) within 50 ft of transmission lines\n- Trees within transmission easement boundaries\n- Trees within 10 ft of utility poles\n- Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment\n- Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment\n- Trees within 20 ft of underground equipment need root barriers\n\nFrom the vision analysis:\n1. Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) shows:\n   - Primarily UNDERGROUND electric infrastructure throughout the site\n   - Overhead electric (OHE) lines shown as dashed lines with \"-OHE-\" text running along the western, southern, and eastern property boundaries\n   - Transformer pads, pull boxes, meters (all underground)\n   - Multiple electric easements noted (5' electric easements, 10' PUE, etc.)\n\n2. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows:\n   - Overhead electric lines along the southern boundary (and western/eastern boundaries)\n   - Four \"M\" (mitigation) trees proposed adjacent to the OHE line at the southern boundary\n   - No clearance dimensions shown\n   - No species identification for the four \"M\" trees at the southern boundary\n   - These trees appear to overlap the OHE line visually on the drawing\n\nThe critical issue is that I need to:\n1. Identify the species of the proposed trees near the OHE\n2. Determine if they are utility-compatible\n3. Check clearances\n4. Cross-reference with ECM Appendix F\n\nThe plant schedule from Sheet 35 shows:\n- 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana)\n\n\n- 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia)\n- 6 Mexican Redbud\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel\n\nHowever, the schedule doesn't indicate which trees are placed where on the landscape plan. The four \"M\" trees positioned near the southern OHE line lack species identification on the drawing itself. I need to work through this systematically: confirm overhead electric infrastructure exists (yes—OHE shown on boundaries), verify trees are proposed near these lines (yes—four M trees near southern OHE), determine their species (unclear without labels), and assess whether clearance dimensions are provided (they're not).\n\nThe plant schedule from Sheet 35 focuses on shade tree calculations and mitigation requirements rather than mapping specific tree locations. Given that 55 inches of mitigation trees are planted on-site with 162 inches still needed, those four M trees near the OHE are likely part of the mitigation planting, making their species selection critical for utility clearance compliance.\n\nThe 12 proposed shade trees (10 Cedar Elm + 2 Live Oak at 4\" caliper each) total 48 inches, leaving only 7 inches of the 55-inch mitigation requirement to be fulfilled by other plantings. The ornamental list includes 2 Texas Mountain Laurel and 6 Mexican Redbud at 45-gallon size, which would add approximately 8 more trees to the mitigation count.\n\nThe critical problem is that the four \"M\" trees along the southern OHE boundary lack species identification on the landscape plan, making it impossible to verify whether they're utility-compatible under ECM Appendix F or meet the clearance requirements in UCM § 1.10.10.4. The plan needs species labels, dimension lines showing clearances, or a keyed plant schedule to resolve this documentation gap. For the non-utility-compatible tree checklist item, I need to confirm whether distribution OHE is present and identify which proposed trees fall within the 15-foot restriction zone. The underground electric line is the primary infrastructure shown, though the overhead electric at the boundary could be either distribution or transmission depending on voltage—a distinction that determines applicable clearance requirements. Without explicit voltage labeling, I can't definitively classify it.\n\nSeveral deficiencies emerge: the landscape plan shows four M trees near the OHE but doesn't specify their species, and the plant schedule doesn't clearly correlate proposed trees to their locations. I can't verify whether large trees (40+ ft mature height) are properly differentiated without knowing what species are actually planted. The relationship between trees and overhead facilities isn't clearly documented on the landscape plan either.\n\nNo clearance dimensions appear anywhere on the plan, so I can't assess whether clearances are measured correctly from conductors or trunks. The applicability of specific standards hinges on whether the OHE is distribution or transmission—EL-2.1 and EL-2.3 apply to distribution lines (which are present), while EL-2.2 and EL-2.4 apply to transmission lines (which I need to confirm).\n\nThe electrical notes don't specify voltage, but the easement widths—5', 10', and 7.5'—suggest distribution rather than transmission infrastructure, which typically requires larger rights-of-way. This means I should treat these as distribution lines and evaluate tree placement against distribution clearance zones: UC trees only within 15 feet, UC or trees under 40 feet mature height between 15-25 feet, and any trees beyond 25 feet. Additionally, no trees should be within 10 feet of poles or pad-mounted equipment, or 5 feet of underground gear.\n\nThe four M-sized trees at the southern overhead line appear to overlap the easement, placing them in restricted zones. However, I'm missing critical information—their species, mature heights, and exact distances from the conductors—that would determine compliance. I need to measure these clearances precisely to assess whether they violate the restrictions. The four M trees lack species labels, which prevents me from verifying compatibility with utility requirements or assessing whether they fall within prohibited zones near the OHE conductor. I can measure the clearance distances using the scale (1\" = 20'), but without species identification, I cannot fully evaluate compliance with EL-2.10 and EL-2.14.\n\nFor the remaining criteria, several items cannot be verified due to missing information: the plant schedule doesn't key species to specific locations (EL-2.1 through EL-2.4), clearances to trees and underground equipment aren't dimensioned (EL-2.12, EL-2.13), and large tree differentiation is impossible without species data (EL-2.11). However, some items appear to pass—no transmission easement is shown (EL-2.5), and depending on tree placement relative to poles and pad-mounts, EL-2.6 and EL-2.7 may comply. Similarly, EL-2.8 and EL-2.9 could pass if no underground equipment is located near proposed trees, and EL-2.15 shows no evidence of non-compliance.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31946,"cache_read_input_tokens":19314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31946},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21547d2b-78a2-4a78-a9a7-593ead7a7df9","uuid":"cca9aa36-2669-487c-a921-01829167900b"}
