er, and storm drain lines require checking the utility plan.\n\n4. **EL-13.24, 13.25, 13.26**: Other underground utilities and potential conflicts.\n\n5. **EL-13.27, 13.28**: Overhead distribution line clearances—need to verify against the utility plan.\n\n6. **EL-13.29, 13.30**: Niche installations.\n\n7. **EL-13.31**: Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances.\n\n8. **EL-13.32**: Grading and drainage requirements for oil-filled equipment.\n\n9. **EL-13.33 through 13.37, 13.39**: Property location, easements, transformer specifications, and customer facility details. I should start by looking at the landscape plan to identify any trees or vegetation that might affect transformer placement.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3389,"cache_read_input_tokens":61675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3389},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ccf424f-5fd8-4631-ab14-3396e8bf729c","uuid":"c098377f-6cf2-4fe2-af58-c305c7f536c8"}
