ng the southern boundary, and multiple trees (labeled \"M\" and \"P\") are proposed directly adjacent to and overlapping this line.\n*   **Western Boundary (Valley View Road):** There are several trees proposed along this boundary (labeled \"**SY**\" and \"**M**\") within shaded areas labeled \"H-1\" and \"H-2\". However, there is no line explicitly labeled \"OHE\" or overhead electric shown on this specific western boundary edge within the provided drawing.\n\n**5. Describe the landscape layout and tree placement relative to utility lines.**\nThe landscape plan utilizes perimeter planting to buffer the property. The most notable interaction with utility lines occurs on the southern edge, where a row of mitigation (\"M\") and parking buffer (\"P\") trees is placed directly parallel and immediately adjacent to the overhead electric (\"---OHE---\") line. The drawn canopies of these proposed trees extend directly over the indicated utility line, suggesting they will grow into the overhead space. Other utility lines like storm drains (\"---SD---\") run through the interior paving areas, with parking lot trees (\"PL\") placed in landscape islands nearby, but the most direct overlap shown is on the southern perimeter."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f67b20d3-b17d-4418-aa28-3e2e17c1cd9f","uuid":"4049d16d-c3c6-4e3a-ba66-fbceae8122df","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here are the answers to your questions:\n\n**1. Where are the overhead electric lines shown on this plan?**\nThe overhead electric lines are indicated by a dashed line labeled \"**---OHE---**\" running along the entire southern boundary (the bottom edge) of the property plan.\n\n**2. Are there any trees or shrubs proposed within 10 feet of the overhead electric lines?**\nYes. Based on the provided scale (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), there are several proposed trees along the southern boundary whose center planting points (indi