{"level":30,"time":1776970749490,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Show all proposed electrical infrastructure on this sheet. Where are underground electric lines routed? Where are transformer pads, electrical meters, and pull boxes located? Are there any overhead electric connections, service drop locations, or clearance dimensions shown? What is the relationship between proposed electrical equipment and existing overhead electric facilities?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" sheet, here is a detailed description of the electrical infrastructure as shown:\n\n### Proposed Electrical Infrastructure Routing\n\nThe proposed electrical system is depicted using bold, continuous blue lines. These lines represent the routing of the underground electrical network throughout the site.\n\n*   **Underground Routing Identification:** Specific segments of these blue lines are explicitly labeled. On the far western edge of the site and centrally near Building 4, callout boxes with leader lines point to the blue line and state EXACTLY: **\"Underground Electric Line\"**.\n*   **Routing Path:** The proposed blue underground line forms a continuous loop or network to serve the buildings.\n    *   It appears to originate on the western side of the property near the \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n    *   It runs north, then turns east, running along the northern section of the driveway/parking area.\n    *   It branches to run south between building clusters (e.g., between Bldg 3/4 and Bldg 4/5).\n    *   It continues along the eastern side of the property, dropping south.\n    *   It runs west along the southern portion of the site, behind Buildings 6, 7, and 8, completing a loop back toward the western side.\n\n### Locations of Electrical Components\n\nSpecific electrical components are indicated by blue symbols and identified with callout boxes containing exact text labels.\n\n**\"Electrical Transformer Pad\" Locations:**\nThese are depicted as blue squares along the underground line routing. There are three identified on this sheet:\n1.  On the western side of the site, near the \"Sidewalk Easement\" and west of Building 2.\n2.  Centrally located, adjacent to the parking area on the west side of Building 4.\n3.  In the southern central area, between the parking areas for Building 7 and Building 8.\n\n**\"Electrical Meters\" Locations:**\nThese are depicted as small blue rectangles, typically located on or immediately adjacent to the building footprints.\n1.  Behind Building 1 (North side).\n2.  Behind Building 3 (North side).\n3.  Behind Building 2 (West side).\n4.  Behind Building 8 (Southwest side).\n5.  Behind Building 7 (South central side).\n6.  On the side of Building 4 (Central).\n7.  Behind Building 5 (East side).\n8.  There is also a label indicating meters near Building 6.\n\n**\"Electrical Pull Box\" Locations:**\nThese are depicted as small blue circles situated at various points along the blue underground lines, often at corners, intersections, or long runs.\n1.  Northwest area, near the property line.\n2.  North central area, near Building 3.\n3.  Northeast corner area.\n4.  East side, near Building 5.\n5.  Southeast area, near Building 6.\n6.  South central area, near Building 7.\n7.  Near the southern property line boundary.\n8.  Southwest area, near Building 8.\n9.  West central area, between Building 2 and Building 8.\n10. West side, near Building 2.\n11. Central area, near Building 4.\n\n### Overhead Connections, Service Drops, and Clearances\n\n*   **Proposed System:** The entire proposed on-site electrical infrastructure (the bold blue lines and components) is indicated as underground.\n*   **Service Drops:** There are no specific labels, distinct line types, or details indicating distinct \"service drop locations\" from an overhead line directly to a building structure. The system appears to transition to underground before distributing to the buildings.\n*   **Clearance Dimensions:** There are no explicit dimensions, notes, or labels shown on this plan view that provide specific clearance requirements (vertical or horizontal) for the electrical equipment.\n\n### Relationship Between Proposed and Existing Facilities\n\nExisting overhead electric lines are indicated by thin black lines with the text marker `---OHE---`.\n\n*   **Western Boundary:** An existing `---OHE---` line runs parallel to the western property line, just outside the site boundary. The proposed blue \"Underground Electric Line\" system begins in close proximity to this line on the west side, suggesting a likely connection or transition point from the existing overhead network to the proposed underground site network, though a specific pole or connection detail is not drawn.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** Another existing line marked `---OHE---` runs along the southern property line. The proposed underground routing runs generally parallel to this boundary on the inside of the site. A proposed \"Electrical Pull Box\" is located in the southeast corner very close to this existing `---OHE---` line.\n*   The plan shows the proposed underground infrastructure navigating around the site, generally staying within the property lines and avoiding conflicts with the existing perimeter overhead lines shown, but specific relationship details (like crossing depths under existing lines) are not provided on this sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1370,"outputTokens":1054,"totalTokens":4718,"reasoningTokens":2294},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou ar