d area). \n*   Existing large tree canopies also overhang the western driveway significantly.\n\n**5. Are there any trees or shrubs shown within 10 lateral feet of the transformer pad locations (Pad 1 NW, Pad 2 W-Central, Pad 3 SW, Pad 4 E-Central, Pad 5 SE)?**\nBecause exact transformer pad footprints are not drawn on this landscape plan, exact measurements cannot be confirmed. However, there is active planting in all of these general zones:\n*   **NW Area:** Contains dense existing tree canopies and newly proposed mitigation (\"M\") trees.\n*   **W-Central Area:** Contains proposed \"SY M\" trees planted immediately adjacent to the driveway.\n*   **SW Area:** Contains proposed trees and existing canopy coverage near the property corner.\n*   **E-Central & SE Areas:** Contain multiple proposed mitigation trees and large existing trees. \n*If the pads are located near the property lines or driveway edges in these zones, it is highly likely that trees or their root zones fall within a 10-foot radius.*\n\n**6. Are there landscape features (groundcover, shrubs) shown near transformer locations?**\nIn the general areas where the pads are reportedly located, the primary landscape features shown are Trees and **SOD**. The landscape plan utilizes Key Note **\"H.7\"** to indicate areas designated for \"SOD\", which covers the vast majority of the unpaved permeable areas in the NW, SW, W-Central, E-Central, and SE zones. No specific shrub symbols or groundcover tables are detailed on this sheet.\n\n**7. Are root barriers indicated for any trees?**\nNo. There are no notes, symbols, or details indicating the use of root barriers on this sheet.\n\n**8. Are there planting details or notes about tree species compatibility with utilities?**\nNo. The provided \"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE\", and \"KEY NOTES\" do not mention utility compatibility, clearance requirements, or safety setbacks for planting near electrical equipment.\n\n**9. What is the distance from planted trees to the nearest paved surfaces/driveways?**\nBased on visual estimation using the provided graphic scale (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), many of the proposed planted trees—particularly the \"SY M\" trees along the western driveway and the \"PL M\" tree in the central island—appear to be planted very close to the pavement edge, roughly **2 to 5 feet** from the nearest paved surface or curb.\n\n**10. Are overhead utility lines or electric easement areas noted on the landscape plan?**\n*   **Overhead Utility Lines:** Yes. There is a dashed line labeled **\"-OHE-\"** (Overhead Electric) running horizontally along the southern property boundary.\n*   **Easements:** No text explicitly labeling a \"Public Utility Easement\" or similar electric easement is visible on this specific sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1579,"outputTokens":1194,"totalTokens":5474,"reasoningTokens":2701},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present