{"level":30,"time":1776970766856,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the Site Plan (Sheet 9) and identify:\n\n1. Are there overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan? If yes, where are they located (north, south, east, west boundary)?\n2. Are there utility poles marked or labeled? If yes, how many and where?\n3. Are there pad-mounted electrical transformers shown? If yes, how many and where are they located?\n4. What is the relationship between proposed trees (if shown) and electrical infrastructure?\n5. Any notes or labels indicating electric facility locations or clearances?\n\nPlease be specific about locations and describe what electrical infrastructure is visible on the overall site plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a close examination of the provided Site Plan (Sheet 9), here are the details regarding the electrical infrastructure:\n\n**1. Are there overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan? If yes, where are they located?**\n*   **Yes.** There is a line style marked with **\"-OHE-\"** running along the entire **southern boundary** of the site. \n\n**2. Are there utility poles marked or labeled? If yes, how many and where?**\n*   **Yes.** There is at least one utility pole explicitly labeled as **\"Power Pole\"**. It is located just off-site in the **northwest corner** area, near the intersection of the street and the site's northern entrance driveway.\n*   A **\"Guy Wire\"** and an **\"AT&T Post\"** are also labeled in this same immediate northwest off-site area.\n\n**3. Are there pad-mounted electrical transformers shown? If yes, how many and where are they located?**\n*   **Yes.** There is one clearly labeled **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** shown on the plan.\n*   It is located on the **west side** of the property, positioned just south of the main entrance driveway and west of Building 1. \n*   *Note: The designation \"(Typ.)\" implies this may be a typical detail for multiple locations, but only this specific one is explicitly pointed out with a text label on this sheet.*\n\n**4. What is the relationship between proposed trees (if shown) and electrical infrastructure?**\n*   Directly adjacent to the labeled \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" on the west side, there is a square feature labeled **\"Tree Well need to look up approp. detail\"**. This indicates a proposed tree location in close proximity to the transformer pad.\n*   Along the southern boundary where the \"-OHE-\" lines run, there are large dashed circles (typically denoting existing tree canopies) that visually overlap the overhead electric line path. However, there are no specific text notes describing conflict mitigation or required trimming. \n\n**5. Any notes or labels indicating electric facility locations or clearances?**\n*   **Electric Easements:** Several specific electrical easements are labeled dictating facility locations/boundaries:\n    *   Along the eastern boundary: **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 F.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   Near the southeastern corner: **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5068, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Clearances:** There are no explicit text notes on this page detailing numerical electrical clearance requirements (e.g., minimum distances from OHE lines).\n*   **Underground Utilities:** The plan includes a **\"Texas 811\"** logo with the text **\"Call Before You Dig!!\"**, which serves as a general warning for locating underground electric and utility facilities prior to construction.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1451,"outputTokens":643,"totalTokens":4596,"reasoningTokens":2502},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Site Plan (Sheet 9) and identify:\n\n1. Are there overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan? If yes, where are they located (north, south, east, west boundary)?\n2. Are there utility poles marked or labeled? If yes, how many and where?\n3. Are there pad-mounted electrical transformers shown? If yes, how many and where are they located?\n4. What is the relationship between proposed trees (if shown) and electrical infrastructure?\n5. Any notes or labels indicating electric facility locations or clearances?\n\nPlease be specific about locations and describe what electrical infrastructure is visible on the overall site plan."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-SQeWDO6fXscZnTrBEI79jYsG","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 18:59:26 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::gx4r9-1776970718462-765c5f69b291"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a close examination of the provided Site Plan (Sheet 9), here are the details regarding the electrical infrastructure:\n\n**1. Are there overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan? If yes, where are they located?**\n*   **Yes.** There is a line style marked with **\"-OHE-\"** running along the entire **southern boundary** of the site. \n\n**2. Are there utility poles marked or labeled? If yes, how many and where?**\n*   **Yes.** There is at least one utility pole explicitly labeled as **\"Power Pole\"**. It is located just off-site in the **northwest corner** area, near the intersection of the street and the site's northern entrance driveway.\n*   A **\"Guy Wire\"** and an **\"AT&T Post\"** are also labeled in this same immediate northwest off-site area.\n\n**3. Are there pad-mounted electrical transformers shown? If yes, how many and where are they located?**\n*   **Yes.** There is one clearly labeled **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** shown on the plan.\n*   It is located on the **west side** of the property, positioned just south of the main entrance driveway and west of Building 1. \n*   *Note: The designation \"(Typ.)\" implies this may be a typical detail for multiple locations, but only this specific one is explicitly pointed out with a text label on this sheet.*\n\n**4. What is the relationship between proposed trees (if shown) and electrical infrastructure?**\n*   Directly adjacent to the labeled \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" on the west side, there is a square feature labeled **\"Tree Well need to look up approp. detail\"**. This indicates a proposed tree location in close proximity to the transformer pad.\n*   Along the southern boundary where the \"-OHE-\" lines run, there are large dashed circles (typically denoting existing tree canopies) that visually overlap the overhead electric line path. However, there are no specific text notes describing conflict mitigation or required trimming. \n\n**5. Any notes or labels indicating electric facility locations or clearances?**\n*   **Electric Easements:** Several specific electrical easements are labeled dictating facility locations/boundaries:\n    *   Along the eastern boundary: **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 F.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   Near the southeastern corner: **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5068, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Clearances:** There are no explicit text notes on this page detailing numerical electrical clearance requirements (e.g., minimum distances from OHE lines).\n*   **Underground Utilities:** The plan includes a **\"Texas 811\"** logo with the text **\"Call Before You Dig!!\"**, which serves as a general warning for locating underground electric and utility facilities prior to construction.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1451,"outputTokens":643,"totalTokens":4596,"reasoningTokens":2502},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"googl