{"level":30,"time":1776970777130,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Show all proposed trees and plantings on this landscape plan. Specifically identify any trees or large shrubs that are planted within 10 feet of overhead electric distribution lines or within 50 feet of overhead electric transmission structures. Note the species of any trees near overhead electric facilities. Are there any trees marked as \"utility compatible\" species that are being used near overhead lines?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided landscape plan sheet (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the analysis regarding your specific requests:\n\n**Proposed Trees and Plantings Overview:**\nThe plan displays numerous proposed trees, indicated by circular canopies with central crosshairs or internal line patterns, distributed primarily along the site's perimeter and within parking islands. Plantings are broadly categorized by area using \"KEY NOTES\" (e.g., shaded areas marked **H.3** for \"STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\", **H.4** for \"PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\", and **H.7** for \"SOD\").\n\n**Trees Near Overhead Electric Lines:**\n*   **Location of OHE:** There is an overhead electric line indicated by a dashed line labeled **\"- OHE -\"** running horizontally along the bottom (southern) property boundary.\n*   **Proximity:** There are several trees proposed in close proximity to this line. While exact measurements aren't explicitly dimensioned for these distances, visually scaling against the 1\"=20'-0\" scale bar suggests they are very close, likely within 10 feet.\n    *   Near the bottom right corner, there is a cluster of at least three proposed trees located directly adjacent to or partially under the \"- OHE -\" line. Two of these nearby trees have small tags labeled **\"M\"**.\n    *   Near the bottom left corner, there is another proposed tree located very close to the \"- OHE -\" line.\n\n**Tree Species Near Overhead Electric Facilities:**\n*   Specific tree species (e.g., Oak, Elm, Crepe Myrtle) are **not listed** on this specific sheet.\n*   The trees are only identified by category tags. According to the text below the Key Notes, the **\"M\"** tag found near the trees by the bottom right OHE line stands for:\n    *   `M - MITIGATION TREE`\n\n**\"Utility Compatible\" Species:**\n*   There are **no notes, tags, or designations** on this sheet indicating that any of the proposed trees are \"utility compatible\" species. A separate plant schedule (likely on a different sheet) would be needed to verify the exact species and whether they meet utility compatibility requirements.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1384,"outputTokens":465,"totalTokens":3326,"reasoningTokens":1477},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on anot