{"level":30,"time":1776970780428,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HthKPk4KKAGsW82vRruvRn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me systematically evaluate all 15 checklist items based on my comprehensive research. Let me create a summary of my findings:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY - Valley View Townhomes Tree/Electric Utility Clearances\n\n**Overhead Infrastructure Present:**\n- OHE (overhead electric) line running along southern boundary\n- OHE line running along western boundary (along Valley View Road)\n- Utility poles present at northwest corner (off-site) and at southern boundary corners\n- Pad-mounted transformer on west side south of Building 1 with adjacent tree well\n- 5' electric easements on eastern boundary\n\n**Proposed Trees:**\n- 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) - 100 GAL, 4\" CAL\n- 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) - 100 GAL, 4\" CAL\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) - 45 GAL, 2.5\" CAL\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) - 45 GAL, 2.5\" CAL\n\n**Critical Measurements (Sheet 31 Landscape Plan):**\n- Southeastern tree to OHE conductor: **3 feet** (FAIL - violates 15 ft distribution min & 10 ft pole min)\n- Southwestern tree to OHE conductor: **13.2 feet** (FAIL - violates 15 ft distribution min)\n- Center-south tree to OHE conductor: **20.9 feet** (PASS for 15 ft, but within 25 ft range for large trees)\n\n**Major Deficiencies Found:**\n1. Landscape plan shows tree symbols but does NOT identify species by location\n2. No clearance dimensions shown on landscape plan\n3. Multiple trees within restricted zones with insufficient clearances\n4. Tree well adjacent to transformer pad with unclear setback\n5. No Austin Energy approval documentation visible\n6. No voltage classification specified for OHE lines\n7. No notes addressing c