{"level":30,"time":1776970790322,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_016k8Xti5mPC1Uj99U5bbSJk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of this site plan, I now have a clear picture of the overhead electric infrastructure and the missing documentation. Let me now compile my findings for the checklist items.\n\n## Summary of Research Findings\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Present:**\n- One overhead electric (OHE) line shown on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31), running along the southern property boundary\n- 5-foot electric easements on property (per facts.md and existing conditions survey)\n- Electric Notes on Sheet 3 acknowledge developer responsibility for maintaining clearances per NESC, OSHA, and City standards\n- Type and voltage of OHE line NOT identified on plans\n\n**Critical Missing Documentation:**\n- NO building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n- NO section/profile plans showing vertical clearances from overhead line to buildings, driveways, or parking\n- NO dimension annotations showing horizontal sky-to-ground (7.5 ft) or radial (15 ft) clearances\n- NO registered surveyor data for conductor locations or mid-span clearances  \n- NO clearance verification for trees near overhead line; species utility-compatibility not verified\n- NO 48-hour notification note (Texas Health & Safety Code § 752.003)\n- Overhead line characteristics (voltage, type: distribution vs. transmission) NOT specified\n\n**Site Features Adjacent to/Near OHE Line:**\n- Buildings 6, 7, 8 on southern portion\n- Retaining walls on southern boundary\n- Driveways and parking areas\n- Extensive landscape plantings including trees\n- Water/wastewater utilities\n- Underground electric infrastructure\n\n**Applicable Standards:**\n- 7.5 ft horizontal sky-to-ground clearance (UCM § 1.10.3)\n- 15 ft radial clearance from distribution conductors (UCM § 1.10.3)\n- 16-18 ft vertical clearance for driveways (UCM § 1.10.6.2)\n- 10 ft lateral clearance for trees with utility-compatible species (ECM § 2.4.1.D, § 2.4.2.C)\n- 48-hour notification requirement (Texas Health & Safety Code Ch. 752)\n\nNow I will output my findings for the deficient items:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_read_input_tokens":76105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2814},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a582675-f45b-4e40-ac49-d1379f357a0d","uuid":"39e3c69f-b919-4d9e-9f00-657a0f0eb5ed"}
