{"level":30,"time":1776970805421,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Identify all transformer pads on the site plan (they appear as rectangular pads, likely labeled from the electrical plan). For each transformer pad, measure and describe: 1) Distance to nearest building edge/wall, 2) Distance to parking areas or driving surfaces, 3) Distance to sidewalks, 4) Distance to retaining walls, 5) Presence of any protective elements (bollards, barriers). Also describe the site layout, building positions, parking configuration, and any clearance dimensions that are dimensioned on the plan. Note the scale of the drawing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here is the detailed information requested:\n\n### Scale\n*   **Scale:** The drawing scale is explicitly noted in the bottom right corner (above the title block) as **Scale 1\" = 20'**.\n\n### Transformer Pad Analysis\nThere is one identifiable rectangular pad explicitly labeled as a transformer pad on this site plan. \n\n**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\n*   **Location:** Situated on the western side of the site, south of the main entrance drive and directly west of Building 2.\n*   **1) Distance to nearest building edge/wall:** The nearest building is Building 2, located to the east. There is no explicit dimension line showing the exact distance from the pad to the building.\n*   **2) Distance to parking areas or driving surfaces:** The pad is located immediately south of the main entrance drive aisle. No explicit clearance dimension is provided between the pad and the driveway edge.\n*   **3) Distance to sidewalks:** The pad is immediately adjacent to (appearing to touch or sit just off the edge of) a walkway labeled \"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ.)\" that runs along its eastern edge.\n*   **4) Distance to retaining walls:** There are no retaining walls in the immediate vicinity of this pad.\n*   **5) Presence of protective elements:** There are no bollards, barriers, or other protective elements labeled or depicted around this transformer pad.\n\n*(Note: While other small rectangular pads exist behind the buildings, none are labeled as transformer pads; they are typically indicative of HVAC units or similar equipment. Bollards are used elsewhere on the site, such as near Building 4 and Building 5, but not at this transformer location.)*\n\n### Site Layout, Building Positions, and Parking Configuration\n*   **Site Layout:** The site is a multi-family residential development featuring a single primary entrance from the west. A central private drive aisle runs east-west through the middle of the property, providing access to all buildings and dead-ending near the eastern boundary. A \"Biofiltration Detention Pond\" is located in the northeast corner of the site. Concrete retaining walls run along portions of the northern, eastern, and southern property boundaries.\n*   **Building Positions:** The site contains exactly 8 buildings, denoted as Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8.\n    *   **North of the drive aisle:** Bldg. 1, Bldg. 3, and Bldg. 5.\n    *   **South of the drive aisle:** Bldg. 2, Bldg. 4, Bldg. 7, and Bldg. 8.\n    *   **Eastern edge:** Bldg. 6 sits at the eastern terminus of the drive.\n*   **Parking Configuration:** Parking consists of integrated garages within the townhome units and surface parking. Several parallel surface parking spaces are visually designated alongside the main central drive aisle. The specific parking counts are detailed in the \"Parking Data\" table transcribed below.\n\n### Clearance Dimensions\nThe following clearance and separation dimensions are explicitly noted on the plan:\n*   **Main Drive Aisle Width:** Dimensioned as **26.1'** near the western entrance (between Bldg 1 and Bldg 2) and **26'** in the central portion (between Bldg 3 and Bldg 4, and near Bldg 5/Bldg 7).\n*   **Entrance Setback:** Dimensioned as **25.8'** from the southern edge of the entrance driveway to Building 2.\n*   **Building Separations:**\n    *   Between Bldg 3 and Bldg 5: **19.3'**\n    *   Between Bldg 2 and Bldg 4: **21.3'**\n    *   Between Bldg 7 and Bldg 8: **10.2'**\n*   **Off-site Driveway Clearance:** \"Distance between Nearest Adjacent Driveway = **228.5'**\" (noted at the western entrance).\n\n***\n\n### Exact Table Transcriptions\nAs requested, here are the exact, character-by-character transcriptions of the tables present on the document.\n\n**Building Data Table**\n| Building # | Building Type | Gross Floor Area (sf) | Building Coverage (sf) | Bedroom Type | Units |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | 4 Plex | 8,550 | 3,290 | Two Bedroom | 16 |\n| 2 | 6 Plex | 13,004 | 4,997 | Three Bedroom | 23 |\n| 3 | 5 Plex | 10,776 | 4,144 | Total Units | 39 |\n| 4 | 5 Plex | 10,776 | 4,144 | | |\n| 5 | 4 Plex | 8,550 | 3,290 | Maximum Number of Building Stories = 3 | |\n| 6 | 4 Plex | 8,550 | 3,290 | | |\n| 7 | 5 Plex | 10,776 | 4,144 | | |\n| 8 | 6 Plex | 13,004 | 4,997 | Foundation = Slab on grade | |\n\n**Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n| Unit Type | Efficiency | 1 Bedroom | 2+ Bedroom |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Number of Units | 0 | 0 | 39 |\n| Required Site Area Per Unit (sf) | 1,600 | 2,000 | 2,400 |\n| Site Area Required (sf) | 0 | 0 | 93,600 |\n| Total Site Area Required (sf) | | | 93,600 |\n| Total Site Area Provided (sf) | | | 94,192 |\n\n**Building Height Table**\n| Building # | Building Type | Average (MSL) | Building Height (FT) | Avg. Building Height (MSL) | Height Allowed (FT) | Height Allowed (MSL) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | 4 Plex | 686.25 | 35' - 10.75\" | 722.15 | 40' | 726.25 |\n| 2 | 6 Plex | 684.50 | 33' - 4.75\" | 717.90 | 40' | 724.50 |\n| 3 | 5 Plex | 685.00 | 36' - 1\" | 721.08 | 40' | 725.00 |\n| 4 | 5 Plex | 684.25 | 33' - 4.75\" | 717.65 | 40' | 724.25 |\n| 5 | 4 Plex | 682.17 | 35' - 10.75\" | 718.07 | 40' | 722.17 |\n| 6 | 4 Plex | 681.75 | 35' - 10.75\" | 717.65 | 40' | 721.75 |\n| 7 | 5 Plex | 682.50 | 33' - 4.75\" | 715.90 | 40' | 722.50 |\n| 8 | 6 Plex | 682.25 | 33' - 4.75\" | 715.65 | 40' | 722.25 |\n\n**Site Data Table**\n| | | | |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Zoning: | MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density | | |\n| Use: Multi-Family Residential | s.f. | acres | % |\n| Site Area: | 94,192 | 2.162 | |\n| Allowable Impervious Cover: | 56,515 | 1.297 | 60% |\n| Existing Impervious Cover: | 61,350 | 1.408 | 65% |\n| Impervious Cover Removed: | 61,350 | 1.408 | 65% |\n| Total Impervious Cover: | 55,502 | 1.274 | 59% |\n| Allowable Building Coverage: | 47,096 | 1.081 | 50% |\n| Proposed Building Coverage: | 32,298 | 0.741 | 34% |\n| Gross Floor Area: | 83,886 | 1.926 | |\n| Building Slab Construction | | Slab On Grade | |\n| Common Open Space Required | 4709.62 | | |\n| Common Open Space provided | 4710 | | |\n\n**Parking Data**\n*(Note: The ADA values appear as the letter 'X')*\n*   Land Use: Residential\n*   Parking Spaces Provided: 10 Surface / 78 Garage\n*   Compact Spaces Provided: 0\n*   ADA Spaces Required: X\n*   ADA Spaces Provided: X\n*   Total Bicycle Spaces Required: 5\n*   Long Term Bicycle Spaces Required: 3\n*   Long Term Bicycle Spaces Provided: 39 (1 per Garage)\n*   Short Term Bicycle Spaces Required: 2\n*   Short Term Bicycle Spaces Provided: 2","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1425,"outputTokens":2230,"totalTokens":10289,"reasoningTokens":6634},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. 