ned directly on the overhead electric line (measured 0-0.8 feet) at the southern property boundary\n2. No species labels on landscape plan for any trees near utilities\n3. Underground electrical equipment shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) but not cross-referenced on landscape plan (Sheet 31)\n4. No clearance dimension lines on landscape plan\n5. No root barrier details or specifications shown\n\nThe findings have been submitted in structured format for regulatory processing.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"21547d2b-78a2-4a78-a9a7-593ead7a7df9","total_cost_usd":0.26126665,"usage":{"input_tokens":143,"cache_creation_input_tokens":98577,"cache_read_input_tokens":442324,"output_tokens":18734,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":98577,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":143,"outputTokens":18734,"cacheReadInputTokens":442324,"cacheCreationInputTokens":98577,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.26126665,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where proposed mitigation trees are located adjacent to overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"}],"comment":"Four mitigation trees are proposed at clearances of 0-0.8 feet from the overhead electric conductor (measured). However, species identification is missing, preventing verification of whether these are non-utility-compatible trees. Without species designation per ECM Appendix F, compliance with the 15-foot minimum clearance requirement for non-utility-compatible trees cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where proposed mitigation trees are located adjacent to overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"}],"comment":"Four mitigation trees are proposed at clearances of 0-0.8 feet from the overhead electric conductor. However, species identification is missing and mature heights are not specified, preventing verification of whether any are large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F). Without species and height information, compliance with the 25-foot minimum clearance requirement for large trees from distribution lines cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary at utility pole locations along overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"}],"comment":"Proposed mitigation trees are positioned at measured clearances of 0-0.8 feet from overhead electric poles/conductors at the southern boundary. Minimum clearance requirement is 10 lateral feet from any electric utility pole. Three of four trees are within or directly on the utility infrastructure."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary (four mitigation trees near OHE); potentially other tree locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Calculations (Sheet 35)"}],"comment":"Four proposed mitigation trees shown on the landscape plan adjacent to the overhead electric line are not identified by species. The landscape plan uses generic symbols (M for mitigation, SY for street yard, PL for parking lot) but does not label individual trees with species codes or names. The plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists shade trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm) and ornamental trees (Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) but does not clearly indicate which species are proposed at which specific locations on the landscape plan. Species identification is required to verify utility compatibility per ECM Appendix F."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary and other areas with proposed trees near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)"}],"comment":"Large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) cannot be differentiated from smaller trees on the landscape plan because species are not identified. Landscape plan and plant schedule lack notation indicating which proposed trees are large-stature species. Without this differentiation, the applicability of large-tree clearance restrictions (25 feet minimum from distribution conductors, 50 feet from transmission) cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where proposed trees are located adjacent to overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentI