{"level":30,"time":1776970810683,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01CSoCVKQLqHDWYqyS5335Wd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The site plan vision only identified ONE transformer pad on Sheet 9. But the electrical plan (Sheet 21) showed 4 transformer pads. This suggests that either:\n1. The site plan doesn't show all transformer pads clearly\n2. The electrical plan and site plan may not be fully coordinated\n\nThis is a significant finding - the electrical plan shows 4 transformers but the site plan only depicts one or doesn't clearly show them.\n\nLet me now measure specific distances from the transformer pads to buildings and other features using the measure-distance tool. First, I need to get more detailed information about clearances.\n\nKey issues identified so far:\n1. **All transformer pads appear to be underneath or adjacent to large tree canopies** - critical for EL-13.13 and EL-13.14\n2. **Transformer pad dimensions are not specified** - needed for EL-13.37 (pad dimensions must match AE Design specs)\n3. **No clearance dimensions dimensioned on electrical plan** - all clearances would need to be measured\n4. **Service type not specified** (single vs three-phase) - needed for some clearance requirements\n5. **No transformer easements shown** - required by EL-13.35\n6. **No AE Design approval documentation visible** - needed for EL-13.4 (reduced clearances) and EL-13.37 (pad dimensions)\n\nLet me now measure specific clearances from transformers. I'll use the measure-distance tool for the key transformers to verify clearances to buildings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2678,"cache_read_input_tokens":55473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_