as with truck traffic) vertical clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Vehicle parking and display areas on southern portion of site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to parked vehicles are not provided on site plans. If parking areas are located beneath or adjacent to the overhead line, plans must include notes and section views specifying the minimum vertical clearance (16 feet for parking without truck traffic or 18 feet with truck traffic) and dimensioning from the lowest overhead conductor to finished parking elevation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All site features near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimension annotations are shown on plans. Where clearance dimensions are eventually provided, they must originate from the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from the utility pole centerline or pole structure. On multi-conductor installations, the outermost conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. All future clearance annotations must clearly show dimension lines extending from the outside conductor to the outermost edge of structures and site features."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash enclosure or receptacle locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance verification for trash enclosures or receptacle locations beneath or near overhead electric facilities is not provided. If trash collection areas are located beneath the overhead line, plans must verify the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance accounting for the height of trash bins when raised during collection service, and provide dimension annotations showing adequate clearance from the outer conductor."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site, specifically buildings and structures on southern portion near overhead electric easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot verify from available plans whether customer facilities are installed directly under or over the overhead distribution line, which is prohibited regardless of clearance distances per UCM § 1.10.3. The overhead electric line characteristics (distribution vs. transmission, voltage level, exact routing path) are not clearly identified on plans with sufficient detail to determine if any structures violate the prohibition against facilities beneath/over distribution lines. Applicant must provide detailed utility plans identifying the overhead line type and voltage, showing its exact routing in plan and profile, and confirming no structures are positioned directly beneath or above it."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions verifying that water meters maintain the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor of existing overhead electric service drops are not provided. If water meters are located on the site, utility plans must show their locations with clearance dimension annotations from any overhead electric service lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions verifying that water lines maintain minimum clearance from existing or proposed overhead electrical distribution facilities are not shown on utility plans. Utility plan and profile sheets must include clearance dimension annotations showing the horizontal and vertical separation between water line routing and overhead electric facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings and site features with proposed elevations ranging from 683 to 687.5 feet on southern portion near overhead line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Registered surveyor mid-span clearance data showing overhead electric conductor elevations is not provided when vertical clearances between overhead facilities and proposed site features (buildings with FFE ranging from 683 to 687.5 feet, driveways, parking) appear to be marginal or insufficient. If clearances appear less than required minimums, applicant must provide surveyed data showing conductor elevation and mid-span measurements confirming adequate vertical clearance from the outer conductor to all site features at their highest points."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed within clearance distance of overhead electric line on southern portion of site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Lateral distance dimensions from proposed tree locations to overhead electric conductors are not shown on landscape plans. Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors (voltage <60kV) are not verified to be from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, species marked 'UC'). Landscape plan must include: (1) measurement of lateral horizontal distance from each tree to the outer conductor; (2) species verification against ECM Appendix F for utility-compatible designation if trees are within 10 feet of distribution conductors or 50 feet of transmission conductors per UCM § 1.10.10.4; and (3) confirmation that only utility-compatible trees are proposed within required clearance distances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads shown on electrical design plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to the top of transformer equipment are not shown on utility plan section views. If transformers are located beneath or adjacent to overhead electric facilities, plans must include section views dimensioning the vertical clearance from the lowest point of overhead conductors to the highest point of transformer equipment to verify the minimum 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site with proposed construction near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. A note must be added to the Cover Sheet or General Notes requiring 48-hour advance notification to Austin Energy before any construction, excavation, or work activities begin in proximity to overhead electric facilities."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_read_input_tokens":76105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2814},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a582675-f45b-4e40-ac49-d1379f357a0d","uuid":"f26e3a05-00f7-4250-b950-cc865b932328"}
