CM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls along southern property boundary near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section views showing clearance dimensions from the outermost electric line to the retaining wall are not provided. Retaining walls are shown on grading and landscape plans along the southern boundary where the overhead electric line is located. Plans must include detailed cross-sections with dimension annotations verifying the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outer conductor to the wall face."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls along southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section exhibits with dimension annotations from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of retaining walls are not included. Although wall plans and details are provided on Sheets 38 and 39, these sections do not show the overhead electric conductor or clearance dimensions required to verify compliance with the 7.5-foot minimum clearance requirement. Applicant must provide sections showing the conductor location and clearance dimensions to wall faces."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and parking areas on southern portion of site near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance dimensions from the lowest point of the overhead electric facilities (including any attachments) to finished driveway grade are not shown on grading plans or section views. If driveways are located beneath or adjacent to the overhead line, plans must include sections showing mid-span clearances verifying the minimum 16-foot (parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot (areas with truck traffic) vertical clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Vehicle parking and display areas on southern portion of site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to parked vehicles are not provided on site plans. If parking areas are located beneath or adjacent to the overhead line, plans must include notes and section views specifying the minimum vertical clearance (16 feet for parking without truck traffic or 18 feet with truck traffic) and dimensioning from the lowest overhead conductor to finished parking elevation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All site features near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimension annotations are shown on plans. Where clearance dimensions are eventually provided, they must originate from the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from the utility pole centerline or pole structure. On multi-conductor installations, the outermost conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. All future clearance annotations must clearly show dimension lines extending from the outside conductor to the outermost edge of structures and site features."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash enclosure or receptacle locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance verification for trash enclosures or receptacle locations beneath or near overhead electric facilities is not provided. If trash collection areas are located beneath the overhead line, plans must verify the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance accounting for the height of trash bins when raised during collection service, and provide dimension annotations showing adequate clearance from the outer conductor."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site, specifically buildings and structures on southern portion near overhead electric easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot verify from available plans whether customer facilities are installed directly under or over the overhead distribution line, which is prohibited regardless of clearance distances per UCM § 1.10.3. The overhead electric line characteristics (distribution vs. transmission, voltage level, exact routing path) are not clearly identified on plans with sufficient detail to determine if any structures violate the prohibition against facilities beneath/over distribution lines. Applicant must provide detailed utility plans identifying the overhead line type and voltage, showing its exact routing in plan and profile, and confirming no structures are positioned directly beneath or above it."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions verifying that water meters maintain the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor of existing overhead electric service drops are not provided. If water meters are located on the site, utility plans must show their locations with clearance dimension annotations from any overhead electric service lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions verifying that water lines maintain minimum clearance from existing or proposed overhead electrical distribution facilities are not shown on utility plans. Utility plan and profile sheets must include clearance dimension annotations showing the horizontal and vertical separation between water line routing and overhead electric facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings and site features with proposed elevations ranging from 683 to 687.5 feet on southern portion near overhead line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Registered surveyor mid-span clearance data showing overhead electric conductor elevations is not provided when vertical clearances between overhead facilities and proposed site features (buildings with FFE ranging from 683 to 687.5 feet, driveways, parking) appear to be marginal or insufficient. If clearances appear less than required minimums, applicant must provide surveyed data showing conductor elevation and mid-span measurements confirming adequate vertical clearance from the outer conductor to all site features at their highest points."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed within clearance distance of overhead electric line on southern portion of site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Lateral distance dimensions from proposed tree locations to overhead electric conductors are not shown on landscape plans. Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors (voltage <60kV) are not verified to be from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, species marked 'UC'). Landscape plan must include: (1) measurement of lateral horizontal distance from each tree to the outer conductor; (2) species verification against ECM Appendix F for utility-compatible designation if trees are within 10 feet of distribution conductors or 50 feet of transmission conductors per UCM § 1.10.10.4; and (3) confirmation that only utility-compatible trees are proposed within required clearance distances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads shown on electrical design plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to the top of transformer equipment are not shown on utility plan section views. If transformers are located beneath or adjacent to overhead electric facilities, plans must include section views dimensioning the vertical clearance from the lowest point of overhead conductors to the highest point of transformer equipment to verify the minimum 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site with proposed construction near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. A note must be added to the Cover Sheet or General Notes requiring 48-hour advance notification to Austin Energy before any construction, excavation, or work activities begin in proximity to overhead electric facilities."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8853ded2-4cc8-4dc0-8dae-59706317fd0a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776971067496,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011zBv8WmZfm7pQZ5KNX7KHN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P88mpsqSPsN1fiFELaUeYX","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary landscape area adjacent to overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows trees planted within 15 feet of overhead electric line (measured 13.2 feet and 3 feet at southern boundary), but plant schedule does not identify tree species at specific landscape plan locations. Cannot verify whether non-utility-compatible species (per ECM Appendix F UC designation) are being installed without species identification on landscape drawing."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary landscape area within 25 feet of overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows multiple trees within 25 feet of overhead electric line, but species are not identified by location on the landscape drawing. Plant schedule includes large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm, both with mature heights exceeding 40 feet per ECM Appendix F), but cannot verify if these large-growing species are being planted in the restricted clearance zones."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeastern corner near utility pole on southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows tree planted at southeastern boundary approximately 3 feet from utility pole, violating the 10-foot minimum lateral clearance requirement from overhead electric utility poles."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["West side of property near Building 1, transformer pad location"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows pad-mounted transformer on west side south of Building 1, with a tree well labeled immediately adjacent. Landscape plan does not provide species identification or specific clearance dimensions to verify compliance with 10-foot minimum setback requirement from pad-mounted equipment."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Interior areas with underground electric utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric lines, pull boxes, and underground connections throughout the site, but the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not overlay or cross-reference underground utility locations. Cannot verify that proposed trees are not planted within 5 feet of underground electric equipment."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Interior landscape areas near underground electric utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan shows underground electric equipment (pull boxes, underground service lines), but the landscape plan and plant schedule do not provide sufficient detail to identify trees within 20 feet of underground equipment or verify that required root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment) are specified in planting details or notes."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary near overhead electric line; West side near transformer pad"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) displays tree symbols near electric facilities but does not identify species by location. Individual trees are labeled only with functional categories (SY, PL, P, M for mitigation), not scientific or common species names. Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists proposed species with quantities but is not cross-referenced on the landscape drawing, preventing verification of which species are installed near utilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary and west side near electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not differentiate large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) from smaller trees. Plant schedule lists proposed species (including Live Oak and Cedar Elm, both exceeding 40-foot mature height) but does not indicate on the landscape drawing which trees are large-growing species, preventing clear identification of trees requiring the more restrictive 25-foot clearance from distribution conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan contains no dimension lines or notes indicating how tree clearances from overhead electric conductors are measured. Without documented measurement methodology on the plans, cannot verify whether clearances are measured from outside conductor (required per UCM 1.10.10.4) or incorrectly from utility pole centerline."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not indicate whether tree clearance measurements are taken from tree trunk center (planting location, required per UCM 1.10.10.4) or from tree canopy edge. Without explicit dimension lines or notes on the landscape drawing specifying measurement reference point, compliance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern and western property boundaries with overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Although landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees and overhead electric line (-OHE-) locations, it does not provide species identification or clearance dimensions necessary to verify compliance with electric utility standards. Reviewers cannot cross-check specific tree species, mature heights, or lateral distances from conductors without supplementary annotations or referenced cross-sections."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary trees within utility clearance zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"ca29fbe6-6361-4580-848e-7807ae462499","label":"Master Comment Report - Electric Review"}],"comment":"Landscape plan shows trees planted within restricted clearance zones from overhead electric infrastructure (within 15 feet of conductors, within 10 feet of poles). No documented written approval letters from Austin Energy authorizing variations to utility clearance standards are visible in the submitted documents. Master Comment Report references Bluebeam platform for Austin Energy detailed review comments, which are not accessible in this documentation set."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1204,"cache_read_input_tokens":77328,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1204},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"970d0b0f-6cb0-49b0-933a-a570c2e8fa2d","uuid":"03cb78cc-68b9-4715-8905-1a809ba42b22"}
