{"level":30,"time":1776971067499,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Look for notes related to overhead electric lines, transmission facilities, and clearance requirements. Specifically:\n1. What electric transmission clearances are specified? (look for any notes about \"25 feet\" or \"20 feet\" mentioned in the guide)\n2. Are there any notes about tree planting near overhead lines or transmission lines?\n3. Is there a 48-hour notification requirement noted for Austin Energy work?\n4. Are there any notes about electric easements or underground/overhead electric service?\n5. Provide the exact text of any electric or transmission clearance notes you find.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan release notes, here are the details regarding overhead electric lines, transmission facilities, and clearance requirements:\n\n**1. Specified Electric Transmission Clearances**\nThe document specifies several 20-foot and 25-foot clearances related to transmission structures in the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" section:\n*   **25 feet:** No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure (Note 1).\n*   **25 feet:** Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors (Notes 2 and 15).\n*   **25 feet:** Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures (Note 14).\n*   **20 feet:** OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction (Note 3).\n*   **20 feet:** Spoils, retaining walls, equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures (Note 8).\n*   **20 feet:** Fire hydrants must be a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure (Note 13).\n\n**2. Notes About Tree Planting Near Overhead/Transmission Lines**\nYes. In the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" section, Note 1 states: \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure.\" \nAdditionally, the \"Electric Notes\" section (Note 1 and a duplicated paragraph below Note 5) states that Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees to keep easements clear, and Note 3 indicates the owner is responsible for initial tree pruning/removal \"within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities\".\n\n**3. 48-Hour Notification Requirement for Austin Energy Work**\nYes. Under \"Electric Transmission Notes,\" Note 3 explicitly states: \"A pre construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting.\"\n\n**4. Notes About Electric Easements or Underground/Overhead Electric Service**\nYes, the \"Electric Notes\" section specifically addresses this in Note 2: \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\" (Note: This exact text is also duplicated in an unnumbered paragraph further down in the same section).\n\n**5. Exact Text of Electric and Transmission Clearance Notes**\n\n*From the \"Electric Notes\" section:*\n*   **Note 4:** \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas State laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n\n*From the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" section:*\n*   **Note 1:** \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n*   **Note 2:** \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading must be sloped to drain away from the transmission structure. Contact Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\"\n*   **Note 3:** \"A pre construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n*   **Note 8:** \"Spoils, retaining walls, equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"\n*   **Note 13:** \"Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\"\n*   **Note 14:** \"Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\"\n*   **Note 15:** \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures (including down guy anchors)\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1431,"outputTokens":1123,"totalTokens":5594,"reasoningTokens":3040},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Look for notes related to overhead electric lines, transmission facilities, and clearance requirements. Specifically:\n1. What electric transmission clearances are specified? (look for any notes about \"25 feet\" or \"20 feet\" mentioned in the guide)\n2. Are there any notes about tree planting near overhead lines or transmission lines?\n3. Is there a 48-hour notification requirement noted for Austin Energy work?\n4. Are there any notes about electric easements or underground/overhead electric service?\n5. Provide the exact text of any electric or transmission clearance notes you find."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-mqWZUqdz40RDlLyCZ5ZdZ43D","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 19:01:06 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::6fwjx-1776970811214-1dbec1dd3e7b"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan release notes, here are the details regarding overhead electric lines, transmission facilities, and clearance requirements:\n\n**1. Specified Electric Transmission Clearances**\nThe document specifies several 20-foot and 25-foot clearances related to transmission structures in the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" section:\n*   **25 feet:** No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure (Note 1).\n*   **25 feet:** Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors (Notes 2 and 15).\n*   **25 feet:** Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures (Note 14).\n*   **20 feet:** OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction (Note 3).\n*   **20 feet:** Spoils, retaining walls, equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures (Note 8).\n*   **20 feet:** Fire hydrants must be a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure (Note 13).\n\n**2. Notes About Tree Planting Near Overhead/Transmission Lines**\nYes. In the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" section, Note 1 states: \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure.\" \nAdditionally, the \"Electric Notes\" section (Note 1 and a duplicated paragraph below Note 5) states that Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees to keep easements clear, and Note 3 indicates the owner is responsible for initial tree pruning/removal \"within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities\".\n\n**3. 48-Hour Notification Requirement for Austin Energy Work**\nYes. Under \"Electric Transmission Notes,\" Note 3 explicitly states: \"A pre construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting.\"\n\n**4. Notes About Electric Easements or Underground/Overhead Electric Service**\nYes, the \"Electric Notes\" section specifically addresses this in Note 2: \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\" (Note: This exact text is also duplicated in an unnumbered paragraph further down in the same section).\n\n**5. Exact Text of Electric and Transmission Clearance Notes**\n\n*From the \"Electric Notes\" section:*\n*   **Note 4:** \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas State laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n\n*From the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" section:*\n*   **Note 1:** \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n*   **Note 2:** \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading must be sloped to drain away from the transmission structure. Contact Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\"\n*   **Note 3:** \"A pre construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n*   **Note 8:** \"Spoils, retaining walls, equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"\n*   **Note 13:** \"Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\"\n*   **Note 14:** \"Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\"\n*   **Note 15:** \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures (including down guy anchors)\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1431,"outputTokens":1123,"totalTokens":5594,"reasoningTokens":3040},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":209024.399456,"endTime":264060.612863,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"O2zqadXsOsmn8eEPstGEkAw"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.052818","marketCost":"0.052818","inferenceCost":"0.052818","inputInferenceCost":"0.002862","outputInferenceCost":"0.049956","generationId":"gen_01KPXVDJ9071ZJ96T5H09581F4"}}},"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided s