{"level":30,"time":1776971077190,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01UVh8xU2LMyBhbFRA3XxePo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have critical information about the electric requirements on the site plan:\n\nKEY FINDINGS:\n1. The site plan has a 48-hour notification requirement for Austin Energy (Electric Transmission Note 3) - this is REQUIRED on plans per UCM § 1.10.2\n2. There are transmission facilities on the site (the notes reference transmission easements, transmission structures, down guy anchors)\n3. The notes mention:\n   - 25-foot clearance from transmission structures for trees, digging, grading\n   - 20-foot clearance for equipment/staging\n   - Owner responsible for maintaining clearances per NESC/OSHA\n   - Owner responsible for tree pruning within 10 feet of overhead electric facilities\n\nNow, this is a critical distinction: The site plan mentions TRANSMISSION facilities (69kV or higher), but earlier we saw OVERHEAD DISTRIBUTION lines mentioned on Sheets 4 and 9 in the ROW. Let me verify whether the site has transmission lines or just distribution lines.\n\nLooking at the earlier findings:\n- Sheet 9 mentioned \"- OHE -\" (Overhead Electric) along the southern boundary in ROW\n- Sheet 4 mentioned utility poles in the ROW\n\nThe transmission notes on Sheet 3 discuss transmission easements, 25-foot clearances, transmission structures, etc. But I need to determine:\n1. Are there transmission lines actually on the site, or just distribution lines?\n2. Are the 25-foot transmission clearances actually applicable, or are distribution clearances applicable?\n\nThe grouping distinguishes between:\n- Distribution (voltage <60kV, typically 12.47kV or 34.5kV in Austin) - requires 7.5 ft sky-to-ground, 15 ft radial, 10 lateral feet for trees\n- Transmission (voltage ≥60kV like 69kV, 138kV, 345kV) - requires different clearances, 50 lateral feet for trees per UCM § 1.10.10.4\n\n\nThe facts.md document references \"5' Electric Easements\" (plat-dedicated), which typically indicate distribution infrastructure rather than transmission—transmission easements are substantially wider. The transmission language on Sheet 3 appears to be standard boilerplate included on all Austin sites with nearby transmission, not necessarily confirming this specific site has transmission lines. I should look for additional electrical design documentation to clarify what type of facility actually exists here.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1508,"cache_read_input_tokens":70150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1508},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f67b20d3-b17d-4418-aa28-3e2e17c1cd9f","uuid":"fcee35e2-99cf-46a3-8945-864684360fee"}
