{"level":30,"time":1776971297856,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","tool":"run_measure_distance","command":"npx tsx /Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/workflows/review/scripts/measure-distance.ts --outputPath='/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/output/measure-distance.json' --reasoning='The project has electric transmission facilities with 25-foot no-dig/no-development zones per Sheet 3 notes. Sheet 9 shows a biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner. The checklist item EL-1.27 prohibits detention ponds in transmission easements. I need to measure the proximity of the proposed detention pond to any transmission structures (poles or guy anchors) to verify if it conflicts with the 25-foot transmission facility clearance requirement.' --applicable_checklist_items='[{\"checklist_id\":\"EL-1.27\",\"checklist_deficiency_text\":\"Customer facilities proposed to be installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities in violation of prohibition, or items within electric easements do not maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor\"}]' --documentId='1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777' --sheetNum='9' --objectPairs='[{\"objectA\":\"Biofiltration/detention pond in northeast corner of site\",\"objectB\":\"Electric transmission pole or guy anchor (if any transmission structures exist on site)\"}]' --scaleInchesPerFoot='0.05'","msg":"Executing typed script tool"}
{"level":30,"time":1776971307424,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01G6ij3kiBPr2ZZ9UKY79mwJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engineer's summary only discusses water and wastewater, not electrical. Let me now do a comprehensive assessment based on what I've found.\n\n## Summary of Research Phase Findings:\n\n**Applicability:** YES - The site has existing overhead electric facilities (OHE) in the right-of-way adjacent to the property\n\n**Key Evidence:**\n1. **Existing Infrastructure:**\n   - Sheet 4 shows overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) running along the southern and western boundaries\n   - Sheet 9 confirms \"- OHE -\" lines running along the southern boundary near Valley View Road\n   - Utility poles exist at property corners\n   - Guy wires are shown on the survey\n   - 5' electric easements are plat-dedicated\n\n2. **Proposed Improvements:**\n   - 8 buildings with various heights and locations\n   - Internal driveways\n   - Parking areas  \n   - Landscaping with trees proposed\n\n3. **Critical Deficiency Found:**\n   - **Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan)** shows trees (labeled \"M\" for Mitigation and \"P\" for Parking Buffer) proposed DIRECTLY adjacent to or overlapping the \"---OHE---\" overhead electric line on the southern boundary\n   - Sheet 35 identifies the proposed trees as:\n     - 10 Cedar Elm\n     - 2 Live Oak\n     - 6 Mexican Redbud (note: vision said 8)\n     - 2 Texas Mountain Laurel\n   - **PROBLEM:** No documentation that these trees meet the ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible (UC) criteria. The landscape plans label them only by functional category (M=Mitigation, P=Parking), not by UC compatibility.\n\n4. **Missing Documentation:**\n   - NO surveyed elevations of overhead conductors on building elevation sheets (no building elevations provided on site plan)\n   - NO section/profile views showing clearances from conductors to buildings\n   - NO vertical clearance dimensions for driveways from overhead lines\n   - NO 48-hour Austin Energy notification note found on cover sheet yet (but Sheet 3 notes mention it's required)\n   - NO clearance dimensions measured from outer conductor (cannot verify they're from conductor vs. pole)\n   - NO specification of whether the overhead lines are distribution or transmission\n   - Trees proposed near overhead lines without UC species verification\n\nNow I need to systematically evaluate each of the 47 checklist items. Several will likely fail or be unverifiable—particularly EL-1.1 regarding building clearances from overhead conductors, since the proposed structures are positioned near the overhead lines but lack the necessary elevation drawings and clearance documentation to confirm compliance.\n\nEL-1.2 requires 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary/neutral conductors for buildings, but without dimension data or conductor type clarification, this cannot be verified. Similarly, EL-1.3 (building projections) and EL-1.6 (buildings near ROW) both fail due to missing elevation details and clearance verification.\n\nEL-1.7 is a clear failure—no building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations were provided. EL-1.8 also fails because the required section and plan exhibits showing conductor-to-building dimensions are absent. For EL-1.9 regarding fence clearances, I can see fence labels on Sheet 4 (\"CRETE FENCE\" and \"WOOD FENCE\"), but no clearance dimensions are shown. EL-1.23 cannot be verified since I cannot confirm whether any existing dimensions are measured from the conductor or the pole.\n\nEL-1.37 addresses trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors needing to be UC species—this is also problematic given the lack of species verification for the proposed landscaping near the overhead lines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":72840,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":442},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f67b20d3-b17d-4418-aa28-3e2e17c1cd9f","uuid":"536b8aef-b2bf-4ec3-9c7f-2bdf326bdb3c"}
