{"level":30,"time":1776971315105,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wiiz1jFc8sc9EKhByu3Jot","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 25 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — Another cross-sectional view labeled 'SECTION B-B VIEW', providing a different vertical perspective of the pipe system and vault, similar to SECTION A-A but showing different components and dimensions.\n     4→\n     5→SECTION B-B VIEW\n     6→\n     7→[Cross-sectional drawing showing a different elevation perspective of the pipe system and vault with annotations for final grade, clearances, and structural details]\n     8→\n     9→## Block 2: diagram — A cross-sectional view labeled 'SECTION A-A VIEW' showing the vertical elevation details of the pipe system and vault from the plan view. It details the final grade, concrete pad dimensions, support stands, and various clearances.\n    10→\n    11→SECTION A-A VIEW\n    12→\n    13→[Cross-sectional drawing showing the elevation of the pipe system and vault with annotations for final grade, clearances, and structural details]\n    14→\n    15→## Block 3: drawing — A detailed plan view drawing showing the layout of a pipe system with various components such as valves, a fire line meter, and strainer within a concrete vault. The drawing includes dimensional annotations and labels indicating components like the 'CITY MAIN', 'CUSTOMER'S VALVE', and '18\" MIN.' clearances.\n    16→\n    17→PLAN VIEW\n    18→\n    19→ALL PIPE FROM CITY MAIN TO CUSTOMER VALVE SHALL BE RESTRAINED DUCTILE IRON\n    20→\n    21→[Plan view drawing of a pipe system within a concrete vault with annotations and callouts pointing to different parts]\n    22→\n    23→## Block 4: notes — A list of eight general notes regarding the construction and installation requirements for the fire line meter and vault, including references to standard specifications, material requirements, clearances, and bedding.\n    24→\n    25→NOTES:\n    26→1. CONCRETE VAULT SHALL NOT BE INSTALLED IN A TRAFFIC AREA.\n    27→2. NUTS AND BOLTS USED TO CONNECT PIPE, FITTINGS AND VALVES SHALL BE STAINLESS STEEL (SS304 OR SS316) OR HIGH-STRENGTH LOW-ALLOY STEEL WITH A BLUE FLUOROPOLYMER FINISH.\n    28→3. FULL FACE 1/8\" THICK RED RUBBER GASKETS USED THROUGHOUT ASSEMBLY.\n    29→4. ALL ITEMS IN MATERIAL LIST, INCLUDING VAULT AND ALL COMPONENTS WITHIN VAULT, TO BE IN COMPLIANCE WITH ITEM No. 512, PRE-CAST WATER UTILITY VAULTS. ALL PIPING, VALVES AND APPURTENANCES OUTSIDE VAULT TO BE SHOWN IN PLAN AND PROFILE SHEET, AND SHALL BE IN COMPLIANCE WITH ITEM Nos. 510 AND 511.\n    30→5. IF NECESSARY, WALL PENETRATION LOCATION IS ALLOWED TO MOVE HORIZONTALLY IN ACCORDANCE WITH SPL WW-298. MINIMUM 18\" CLEARANCE SHALL BE PROVIDED BETWEEN VAULT WALL AND BYPASS PIPING OR FIRE LINE METER COMPONENTS, UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE.\n    31→6. ALL BURIED PIPE AND FITTINGS SHALL BE BEDDED, BACKFILLED, AND WRAPPED IN POLYETHYLENE ENCASEMENT IN ACCORDANCE WITH COA STANDARDS.\n    32→7. THE TOP OF THE VAULT SHALL BE AT AN ELEVATION SUCH THAT THE SURROUNDING GROUND SLOPES AWAY FROM THE VAULT. ADDITIONAL DRAINAGE CONSIDERATIONS SUCH AS CONNECTION OF VAULT DRAINAGE TO STORM SEWER, LATERAL DRAIN LINES FROM GRAVEL FLOOR, OR OTHER MEANS SHALL BE REQUIRED IF CONDITIONS CAUSE WATER TO COLLECT IN VAULT.\n    33→8. BYPASS AND MAIN PIPE SHALL BE SAME DIAMETER.\n    34→\n    35→## Block 6: table — A table providing a schedule for vault dimensions based on the fire line meter size. It includes the vault size (inside dimension) and the offset dimension for 6\", 8\", and 10\" meter sizes.\n    36→\n    37→VAULT SCHEDULE\n    38→\n    39→| FIRE LINE METER SIZE | VAULT SIZE (INSIDE DIMENSION) | OFFSET DIMENSION |\n    40→|---|---|---|\n    41→| 6\" | 8' x 12' | 3'-0\" |\n    42→| 8\" | 10' x 12' | 3'-6\" |\n    43→| 10\" | 10' x 15' | 3'-6\" |\n    44→\n    45→## Block 7: table — A table detailing the materials required for the 6\", 8\" or 10\" Sensus Omni F2 Fire Line Meter installation. It lists items by number, description, size, and type.\n    46→\n    47→6\", 8\" OR 10\" SENSUS OMNI F2 FIRE LINE METER MATERIAL LIST\n    48→\n    49→| ITEM | DESCRIPTION | SIZE | TYPE |\n    50→|---|---|---|---|\n    51→| 1 | FIRE LINE METER AND STRAINER (PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER) | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n    52→| 2 | DISMANTLING JOINT PER COA SPL WW-27J | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n    53→| 3 | RESILIENT-SEATED GATE VALVE (w/HAND WHEEL) PER COA SPL WW-700 | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n    54→| 4 | TEE PER COA SPL WW-27C | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n    55→| 5 | 90° BEND PER COA SPL WW-27C | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n    56→| 6 | DUCTILE IRON CLASS 53 PIPE PER COA SPL WW-27E | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n    57→| 7 | DUCTILE IRON CLASS 53 PIPE PER COA SPL WW-27E | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x PE |\n    58→| 8 | PIPE SADDLE SUPPORT AND STANCHION PER COA SPL WW-614B (USE 5/8\" DIA. x 8\" LONG STAINLESS STEEL WEDGE-ALL ANCHOR, TYP.) | NA | NA |\n    59→| 9 | LINK-SEAL MODULAR SEALS SERIES: LS-525 FOR 6\" PIPE, LS-500 FOR 8\" PIPE AND LS-650 FOR 10\" PIPE w/STAINLESS STEEL HARDWARE, OR EQUAL | NA | NA |\n    60→| 10 | 48\" x 72\" ACCESS HATCH PER COA SPL WW-614A | NA | NA |\n    61→| 11 | CONCRETE VAULT PER COA SPL WW-298 (SEE VAULT SCHEDULE) | NA | NA |\n    62→\n    63→## Block 8: text_block — A disclaimer stating that the engineer/architect assumes responsibility for appropriate use of this standard and that modifications are prohibited.\n    64→\n    65→THE ENGINEER/ARCHITECT ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD. MODIFICATIONS TO THIS STANDARD ARE PROHIBITED.\n    66→\n    67→## Block 9: text_block — A signature block with the name JEFF A. KYLE, likely the approving authority for the standard drawing.\n    68→\n    69→JEFF A. KYLE\n    70→\n    71→## Block 10: text_block — Text indicating the adoption date of the standard as 03/10/2025.\n    72→\n    73→03/10/2025\n    74→ADOPTED\n    75→\n    76→## Block 11: text_block — A block indicating the standard number '512-AW-02' and that it is sheet '1 OF 1'.\n    77→\n    78→STANDARD NO.\n    79→512-AW-02\n    80→1 OF 1\n    81→\n    82→## Block 12: text_block — Text identifying the standard as belonging to the City of Austin, Austin Water department.\n    83→\n    84→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    85→AUSTIN WATER\n    86→\n    87→## Block 14: text_block — The title of the standard drawing indicating it covers 6\", 8\", and 10\" fire line meters.\n    88→\n    89→6\", 8\" AND 10\" FIRE LINE METER\n    90→\n    91→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8749633-cddc-4008-9f86-e2f0ef414315","uuid":"b4e52946-00d7-4716-9981-cc84a8a8b292","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 25 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — Another cross-sectional view labeled 'SECTION B-B VIEW', providing a different vertical perspective of the pipe system and vault, similar to SECTION A-A but showing different components and dimensions.\n\nSECTION B-B VIEW\n\n[Cross-sectional drawing showing a different elevation perspective of the pipe system and vault with annotations for final grade, clearances, and structural details]\n\n## Block 2: diagram — A cross-sectional view labeled 'SECTION A-A VIEW' showing the vertical elevation details of the pipe system and vault from the plan view. It details the final grade, concrete pad dimensions, support stands, and various clearances.\n\nSECTION A-A VIEW\n\n[Cross-sectional drawing showing the elevation of the pipe system and vault with annotations for final grade, clearances, and structural details]\n\n## Block 3: drawing — A detailed plan view drawing showing the layout of a pipe system with various components such as valves, a fire line meter, and strainer within a concrete vault. The drawing includes dimensional annotations and labels indicating components like the 'CITY MAIN', 'CUSTOMER'S VALVE', and '18\" MIN.' clearances.\n\nPLAN VIEW\n\nALL PIPE FROM CITY MAIN TO CUSTOMER VALVE SHALL BE RESTRAINED DUCTILE IRON\n\n[Plan view drawing of a pipe system within a concrete vault with annotations and callouts pointing to different parts]\n\n## Block 4: notes — A list of eight general notes regarding the construction and installation requirements for the fire line meter and vault, including references to standard specifications, material requirements, clearances, and bedding.\n\nNOTES:\n1. CONCRETE VAULT SHALL NOT BE INSTALLED IN A TRAFFIC AREA.\n2. NUTS AND BOLTS USED TO CONNECT PIPE, FITTINGS AND VALVES SHALL BE STAINLESS STEEL (SS304 OR SS316) OR HIGH-STRENGTH LOW-ALLOY STEEL WITH A BLUE FLUOROPOLYMER FINISH.\n3. FULL FACE 1/8\" THICK RED RUBBER GASKETS USED THROUGHOUT ASSEMBLY.\n4. ALL ITEMS IN MATERIAL LIST, INCLUDING VAULT AND ALL COMPONENTS WITHIN VAULT, TO BE IN COMPLIANCE WITH ITEM No. 512, PRE-CAST WATER UTILITY VAULTS. ALL PIPING, VALVES AND APPURTENANCES OUTSIDE VAULT TO BE SHOWN IN PLAN AND PROFILE SHEET, AND SHALL BE IN COMPLIANCE WITH ITEM Nos. 510 AND 511.\n5. IF NECESSARY, WALL PENETRATION LOCATION IS ALLOWED TO MOVE HORIZONTALLY IN ACCORDANCE WITH SPL WW-298. MINIMUM 18\" CLEARANCE SHALL BE PROVIDED BETWEEN VAULT WALL AND BYPASS PIPING OR FIRE LINE METER COMPONENTS, UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE.\n6. ALL BURIED PIPE AND FITTINGS SHALL BE BEDDED, BACKFILLED, AND WRAPPED IN POLYETHYLENE ENCASEMENT IN ACCORDANCE WITH COA STANDARDS.\n7. THE TOP OF THE VAULT SHALL BE AT AN ELEVATION SUCH THAT THE SURROUNDING GROUND SLOPES AWAY FROM THE VAULT. ADDITIONAL DRAINAGE CONSIDERATIONS SUCH AS CONNECTION OF VAULT DRAINAGE TO STORM SEWER, LATERAL DRAIN LINES FROM GRAVEL FLOOR, OR OTHER MEANS SHALL BE REQUIRED IF CONDITIONS CAUSE WATER TO COLLECT IN VAULT.\n8. BYPASS AND MAIN PIPE SHALL BE SAME DIAMETER.\n\n## Block 6: table — A table providing a schedule for vault dimensions based on the fire line meter size. It includes the vault size (inside dimension) and the offset dimension for 6\", 8\", and 10\" meter sizes.\n\nVAULT SCHEDULE\n\n| FIRE LINE METER SIZE | VAULT SIZE (INSIDE DIMENSION) | OFFSET DIMENSION |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6\" | 8' x 12' | 3'-0\" |\n| 8\" | 10' x 12' | 3'-6\" |\n| 10\" | 10' x 15' | 3'-6\" |\n\n## Block 7: table — A table detailing the materials required for the 6\", 8\" or 10\" Sensus Omni F2 Fire Line Meter installation. It lists items by number, description, size, and type.\n\n6\", 8\" OR 10\" SENSUS OMNI F2 FIRE LINE METER MATERIAL LIST\n\n| ITEM | DESCRIPTION | SIZE | TYPE |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | FIRE LINE METER AND STRAINER (PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER) | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n| 2 | DISMANTLING JOINT PER COA SPL WW-27J | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n| 3 | RESILIENT-SEATED GATE VALVE (w/HAND WHEEL) PER COA SPL WW-700 | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n| 4 | TEE PER COA SPL WW-27C | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n| 5 | 90° BEND PER COA SPL WW-27C | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n| 6 | DUCTILE IRON CLASS 53 PIPE PER COA SPL WW-27E | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\n| 7 | DUCTILE IRON CLASS 53 PIPE PER COA SPL WW-27E | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x PE |\n| 8 | PIPE SADDLE SUPPORT AND STANCHION PER COA SPL WW-614B (USE 5/8\" DIA. x 8\" LONG STAINLESS STEEL WEDGE-ALL ANCHOR, TYP.) | NA | NA |\n| 9 | LINK-SEAL MODULAR SEALS SERIES: LS-525 FOR 6\" PIPE, LS-500 FOR 8\" PIPE AND LS-650 FOR 10\" PIPE w/STAINLESS STEEL HARDWARE, OR EQUAL | NA | NA |\n| 10 | 48\" x 72\" ACCESS HATCH PER COA SPL WW-614A | NA | NA |\n| 11 | CONCRETE VAULT PER COA SPL WW-298 (SEE VAULT SCHEDULE) | NA | NA |\n\n## Block 8: text_block — A disclaimer stating that the engineer/architect assumes responsibility for appropriate use of this standard and that modifications are prohibited.\n\nTHE ENGINEER/ARCHITECT ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD. MODIFICATIONS TO THIS STANDARD ARE PROHIBITED.\n\n## Block 9: text_block — A signature block with the name JEFF A. KYLE, likely the approving authority for the standard drawing.\n\nJEFF A. KYLE\n\n## Block 10: text_block — Text indicating the adoption date of the standard as 03/10/2025.\n\n03/10/2025\nADOPTED\n\n## Block 11: text_block — A block indicating the standard number '512-AW-02' and that it is sheet '1 OF 1'.\n\nSTANDARD NO.\n512-AW-02\n1 OF 1\n\n## Block 12: text_block — Text identifying the standard as belonging to the City of Austin, Austin Water department.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nAUSTIN WATER\n\n## Block 14: text_block — The title of the standard drawing indicating it covers 6\", 8\", and 10\" fire line meters.\n\n6\", 8\" AND 10\" FIRE LINE METER\n\n","numLines":91,"startLine":1,"totalLines":91}}}
