hat do not require the services of an engineer.\"\n*   \"A fee in-lieu of parkland dedication must be paid for 39 residential units prior to the issuance of the Certificate of Occupancy. No Certificate of Occupancy may be issued for this development until receipt of payment. Contact the Parks and Recreation Department prior to requesting inspections.\"\n*   \"If at any time during construction of this project an underground storage tank (UST) is found, construction in that area must stop until a City of Austin UST Construction Permit is applied for and approved. Any UST removal work must be conducted by a UST Contractor that is registered with the Texas Commission on Environmental Quality (TCEQ). Contact UST@austintexas.gov if you have any questions.(COA Title 6)\"\n\n**Traffic Control Plan Note (located in the bottom right corner):**\n> **Traffic Control Plan Note:**\n> This note is being placed on the plan set in the absence of a temporary traffic control plan (TCP) with the full understanding that an engineered TCP shall be reviewed and approved by the Right of Way Management Division. Furthermore, a TCP shall be submitted to TCPReview@austintexas.gov for review a minimum of 6 weeks prior to the start of construction. The applicant/project representative further recognizes that a TCP review fee is required for the initial review and all re- reviews, as prescribed by the most current version of the City's fee ordinance.\n> \n> The following must be taken into consideration:\n> - Refer to the Mobility Guidelines for developing traffic control strategies\n>   http://www.austintexas.gov/page/mobility-guidelines\n> - TCPs shall not be approved without an approved site plan, site plan exemption, or general permit.\n> - A traffic control plan is not a permit.\n\n**Small standalone note box (located near the bottom center right):**\n*   \"The proposed stacked biofiltration/detention pond will be privately maintained.\"\n\n### 2. Is there a note about notifying Austin Energy 48 hours before work begins near overhead electric lines?\n**No.** Based on a thorough review of the text on this specific cover sheet, there is no mention of notifying Austin Energy 48 hours prior to work beginning near overhead electric lines.\n\n### 3. Are there notes about owner responsibility for maintaining electrical clearances?\n**No.** There are notes assigning owner responsibility for maintaining drainage/detention ponds and private fire hydrants, but there are no notes regarding owner responsibility for maintaining electrical clearances on this cover sheet.\n\n### 4. What other electrical or utility-related notes are on this cover sheet?\nAside from the \"Sheet List Table\" which lists \"Utility Tap Plan & Profile\" (Sheet 20) and \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21) indicating these exist elsewhere in the set, the only utility-related notes explicitly written on this cover page pertain to water/wastewater and underground storage tanks:\n\n**Water/Wastewater Utility Note:**\n> \"City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\nThis project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin Fire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of this obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced, maintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project includes __1__ private hydrants.\"\n\n**Potable Water Components Note:**\n> \"All potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, shall be essentially \"lead free\" according to the US Safe Drinking Water Act. Examples are valves (corporation stop, curb stop, and pressure reducing), nipples, bushings, pipe, fittings and backflow preventers. Fire hydrants, tapping saddles and 2 inch and larger gate valves are the only components exempt from this requirement. Components that are not clearly identified by the manufacturer as meeting the requirement either by markings on the component or on the packaging shall not be installed.\"\n\n**Underground Utility/Storage Tank Note:**\n> \"If at any time during construction of this project an underground storage tank (UST) is found, construction in that area must stop until a City of Austin UST Construction Permit is applied for and approved. Any UST removal work must be conducted by a UST Contractor that is registered with the Texas Commission on Environmental Quality (TCEQ). Contact UST@austintexas.gov if you have any questions.(COA Title 6)\"\n\n### 5. Are there notes about overhead electric line proximity and safety precautions?\n**No.** There are no notes visible on this cover sheet concerning overhead electric line proximity or safety precautions. (As noted in the instructions, this does not guarantee they are missing from the entire plan set, only that they are absent from this specific cover page)."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776971360132,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JQhMphQU6RpRWWzNR6K7LV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014eStiqEPm3EkpvMWwBVo67","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad clearances and reduced clearance conditions cannot be verified. No explicit clearance dimensions are provided on the electrical plan. If any clearances less than 5 feet to buildings are present, Austin Energy Design written approval, verification of 3-hour fire rating, confirmation that locations are not in confined space, and adequate vertical clearances to windows/doors must be documented but are not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations (northwest near Bldg 2, east central between Bldgs 4-5, southwest near Bldg 8, southeast between Bldgs 6-7)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted transformers cannot be verified as utility-compatible. All four transformer pads are drawn underneath or immediately adjacent to large existing tree canopies. While the tree list identifies species present on-site including Live Oak, Hackberry, Cedar Elm, and Pecan (marked as Appendix F compliant with \"Y\"), the plan does not specify which trees are within 10 feet of each transformer pad or confirm their utility compatibility. No tree species call-outs are provided on the electrical or landscape plans adjacent to transformer locations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Shrub and low-lying vegetation clearances from transformer pads cannot be verified. The landscape plan does not identify specific shrub/vegetation planting locations relative to transformer access door sides. Clearance requirements of 10 feet from access door side and 5 feet from other sides cannot be confirmed from available plans. Transformer access door orientations are not marked on electrical plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment lack documented root barriers. The landscape plan does not identify specific trees within 20 feet of transformers or show root barrier details (minimum 4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment). Although large trees exist proximate to all four transformer pads, no root barrier details or specifications are provided on any plan sheets."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings demonstrating vertical clearances in access paths are not provided. No cross-section sheets show vertical clearances from transformer pads to overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas. Vertical clearance compliance for transformer access cannot be verified from available plan documents."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs dry-type) is not specified on electrical plans. If oil-filled transformers are proposed, grading plan surface drainage direction must slope away from transformer pads. Current grading plans do not indicate drainage direction relative to transformer locations, and equipment type specification is absent from plans, preventing verification of this requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on site plan or plat. Required easements around transformer pads for Austin Energy accessibility are not depicted on the plat (Sheet 2), site plan (Sheet 9), or electrical plan (Sheet 21). Easement width required by Austin Energy Design cannot be determined from submitted plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions do not match or reference Austin Energy Design-approved specifications. Transformer pad dimensions are not dimensioned or labeled on electrical plans. No AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets, specifications, or ESPA documentation is included in the site plan or supplementary documents. Service type (single-phase or three-phase) is not specified, preventing verification of compliance with AE Design requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle routes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bollards are not shown or specified on electrical plans. If transformer pads are installed within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle circulation routes, required 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts (bollards) per AE Design equipment pad details are not depicted or dimensioned on the electrical plan. No AE Design equipment pad details showing bollard specifications are provided with the submittal."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":434,"cache_read_input_tokens":71675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":434},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8749633-cddc-4008-9f86-e2f0ef414315","uuid":"74e01b81-be71-4482-bb73-0f0cfe166318"}
