{"level":30,"time":1776971406151,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JdqFakkRhMFqMchJLiEmp2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the site plan, I can now evaluate all checklist items. Let me prepare the structured findings output with the deficiencies I've identified.\n\nI've found that the project has overhead electric lines (OHE) adjacent to the property in the right-of-way along Valley View Road and the southern boundary, as shown on Sheets 4 and 9. The site includes proposed buildings, driveways, parking areas, landscaping, and other customer facilities that must maintain required clearances.\n\nThe critical deficiencies I've identified are:\n\n1. **Missing building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations** (EL-1.7, EL-1.8) - No building elevations showing surveyed overhead conductor locations and clearance dimensions are provided.\n\n2. **Trees proposed near overhead lines without UC compatibility documentation** (EL-1.37) - Sheet 31 shows trees (labeled M and P) positioned directly on or overlapping the overhead electric line along the southern boundary, with no documentation that these species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) meet ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible requirements.\n\n3. **Multiple clearance verification gaps** - No clearances are dimensioned from conductors to buildings, driveways, parking, fences, or other structures.\n\nLet me now return the findings in the required format:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2823,"cache_read_input_tokens":75810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2823},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_availab