{"level":30,"time":1776971415560,"pid":55640,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":19,"prompt":"Identify water, wastewater, and storm drain line routing on this utility plan. Specifically: 1) Are transformer pad locations shown or referenced? 2) Are there clearance dimensions dimensioned between utility lines and transformer locations? 3) What is the scale? 4) Are utility line locations specifically labeled with call-outs showing distance from transformer pads? Note: Transformers should be at least 5 feet from water, sewer, and storm drain lines per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided utility plan, here is the information regarding the water, wastewater, and storm drain line routing, along with the specific answers to your questions:\n\n**Utility Line Routing Identification:**\n*   **Water Lines (`W`):** Proposed water lines (depicted as thicker lines, colored purple) route throughout the site, entering from the west (\"Existing 8\" Water Line\") and looping around the proposed buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) to provide service.\n*   **Wastewater Lines (`WW`):** Proposed wastewater lines (depicted as blue lines with flow arrows and cleanout markers) route from the buildings to a main line that runs west and connects to an \"Existing #15466 Wastewater MH\" on the left side of the plan.\n*   **Storm Drain Lines (`SD`):** Proposed storm drain lines (depicted as green lines labeled `SD`) route centrally through the site's drive aisles and towards the eastern property boundary. \n\n**Answers to Specific Questions:**\n\n1.  **Are transformer pad locations shown or referenced?**\n    No. While the \"Legend\" in the top right corner explicitly lists a symbol for a \"**Transformer Pad**\" (a square), a thorough scan of the entire site layout reveals that there are no transformer pads actually drawn, placed, or referenced anywhere on this specific utility plan sheet. Similarly, there are no \"Proposed Underground Electric\" (`E`) lines depicted on the drawing. \n2.  **Are there clearance dimensions dimensioned between utility lines and transformer locations?**\n    No. Because there are no transformer pads shown on this plan, there are no clearance dimensions provided between the utility lines (water, sewer, storm drain) and any transformer locations.\n3.  **What is the scale?**\n    The scale is explicitly labeled in the top right corner, directly beneath the graphic scale bar, exactly as:\n    `Scale 1\" = 20'`\n4.  **Are utility line locations specifically labeled with call-outs showing distance from transformer pads?**\n    No. There are no call-outs or labels indicating distances between utility lines and transformer pads, as the transformer pads themselves are completely absent from this sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1416,"outputTokens":472,"totalTokens":3880,"reasoningTokens":1992},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2591576]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single su